Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: God bless you always.

asr-000038
00:03:58.660 --> 00:03:59.540
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

asr-000039
00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.800
Rep. Ivan Howard A. Guintu: Moment of suspension, Madam Speaker.

asr-000040
00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:02.940
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Session suspended.

asr-000054
00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:55.300
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Session is resumed. Majority Leader.

asr-000054-split-2
00:10:55.300 --> 00:11:03.450
Rep. Manuel "Wowo" L. Fortes Jr.: Madam Speaker, I move to consider the proposed budget of the Commission on Human Rights.

asr-000054-split-3
00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:06.440
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Is there any objection? The Chair hears none. The motion is approved. Majority Leader.

asr-000054-split-4
00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:23.100
Rep. Manuel "Wowo" L. Fortes Jr.: Madam Speaker, may we acknowledge the heads and officials of the Commission on Human Rights, namely the Chairperson, Attorney Richard P. Palpal-latoc, Commissioners Attorney Beda A. Epres,

asr-000055
00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:53.100
Rep. Manuel "Wowo" L. Fortes Jr.: Attorney Faydah M. Dumarpa, Justice Monina A. Zenarosa, Judge Maria Amifaith S. Fider-Reyes, together with Executive Director Attorney Jacqueline Ann C. de Guia and Human Rights Violations Victims' Memorial Commission Acting Executive Director Lawrence Charles E. Salazar.

asr-000056
00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:59.230
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: We acknowledge the presence of the heads and staff of the Commission on Human Rights. Welcome to the House of Representatives. Majority Leader.

asr-000056-split-2
00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:17.000
Rep. Manuel "Wowo" L. Fortes Jr.: Madam Speaker, I move that we open the period of sponsorship and debate, and I move to recognize the sponsor, Vice Chair Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez of Alona Partylist.

asr-000056-split-3
00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:23.100
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Is there any objection? The Chair hears none. The period of sponsorship and debate is now open, and we recognize the sponsor

asr-000057
00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:35.230
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: The budget of the Commission on Human Rights, in the person of Vice Chairperson of Appropriations Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez of Alona Partylist. You may now proceed.

asr-000057-split-2
00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:53.100
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleagues in the House of Representatives, magandang gabi po sa ating lahat. I rise today to sponsor the fiscal year 2027 budget of the Commission on Human Rights, an independent constitutional institution trusted with protecting the dignity and fundamental rights of every Filipino.

asr-000058
00:12:53.120 --> 00:13:23.100
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Madam Speaker, allow me to put the CHR budget in perspective through one figure: 0.02%. Out of proposed 7.2 trillion national budget, only PHP 1.273 billion, or around 0.02%, is provided for the CHR under the National Expenditure Program. The Commission proposed 2.749 billion.

asr-000059
00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:53.100
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Even if Congress were to provide the entire amount, it would only represent around 0.04% of the national budget, from 0.02% to 0.04%. Napakaliit po ng hinihingi ng CHR, but it can make a meaningful difference in its ability to investigate human rights violations, assist victims, prevent abuse, and protect the rights of our people.

asr-000060
00:13:53.120 --> 00:14:23.100
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: We cannot continue asking the CHR to do more without giving it the resources necessary to fulfill its constitutional mandate. The CHR is not an adversary of government. Kakampi po natin ang CHR sa mabuting pamamahala. A stronger and independent CHR strengthens accountability, protects the vulnerable, and helps build public trust in our institution. Madam Speaker,

asr-000061
00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:52.200
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: 0.1% is a modest investment for our institution mandated to safeguard the rights of 100% of our Filipino people. For this reason, I respectfully urge this august chamber to support the approval and augmentation of the fiscal 2027 budget of the Commission on Human Rights. Maraming salamat po, Madam Speaker, and I am now ready to take questions from our distinguished

asr-000062
00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:52.960
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: colleagues.

asr-000064
00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:56.350
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Majority Leader.

asr-000065
00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:07.440
Rep. Manuel "Wowo" L. Fortes Jr.: Madam Speaker, I move that we recognize the Honorable Iris Marie de Mesa Montes of 4K Partylist to interpellate on the proposed budget.

asr-000066
00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:15.080
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Representative Iris Marie de Mesa Montes of 4K Partylist is now recognized for her interpolation.

asr-000067
00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:23.920
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you Madam Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor, the Commission on Human Rights Family. Magandang gabi po sa inyong lahat.

asr-000068
00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:38.080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Unang katanungan ko po, would the Commission agree that the credibility of the Philippines' human rights institutions is itself an important component of the country's credibility in the international community?

asr-000069
00:15:39.780 --> 00:15:40.980
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Yes po Madam Speaker.

asr-000070
00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:44.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you Madam Sponsor, Madam Speaker.

asr-000071
00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:52.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: The recent failure of our country's bid for a non-permanent seat in the United Nations Security Council,

asr-000072
00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:53.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: losing

asr-000073
00:15:53.920 --> 00:16:00.620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: the Asia-Pacific contest to Kyrgyzstan in June 2026 has been interpreted by some as a human rights warning.

asr-000074
00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:08.780
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: In fact, prominent international human rights organizations including the International Coalition for Human Rights in the Philippines

asr-000075
00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:19.840
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: have publicly interpreted this electoral setback as a direct reflection of ongoing concerns regarding our domestic human rights record,

asr-000076
00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:23.520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: especially during the Duterte administration.

asr-000077
00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:26.920
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Does the Sponsor share this view?

asr-000078
00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:29.480
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Yes, Madam Chair.

asr-000079
00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:39.060
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: What role exactly did this unresolved human rights violation, especially in the past administration, play in this outcome?

asr-000080
00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:08.700
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Madam Chair,

asr-000081
00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:15.360
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: one of the Commission's significant accomplishments has been the implementation of the Task Force on Zero Backlog Cases,

asr-000082
00:17:16.100 --> 00:17:22.440
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: which substantially reduced the number of pending cases and helped clean up and reconcile our case data.

asr-000083
00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:23.900
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: In particular,

asr-000084
00:17:23.920 --> 00:17:29.740
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: the Commission has identified 493 cases for reinvestigation in 2024,

asr-000085
00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:36.560
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: and the Task Force has directed of 289 cases reinvestigated in 2025.

asr-000086
00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:45.540
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Of these 289 reinvestigated cases, 140 cases are currently for disposition by the TF.

asr-000087
00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:52.540
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: The Task Force also successfully reviewed and evaluated these cases identified for reinvestigation,

asr-000088
00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:57.060
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: and has begun drafting the corresponding resolution for disposition.

asr-000089
00:17:57.720 --> 00:18:05.900
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: This process remains ongoing, with the Commission committed to completing the disposition of these cases by the end of the year, Madam Chair.

asr-000090
00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:10.520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Madam Chair, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-000091
00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:16.260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yung mga binanggit niyo po ay mga accomplishments po ba yan ng CHR?

asr-000092
00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:17.420
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Yes po, Madam Chair.

asr-000093
00:18:17.420 --> 00:18:22.520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: But I was actually trying to find out if, when I asked a while ago,

asr-000094
00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:27.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: if the Human Rights Record of the Philippines, as seen by the international community,

asr-000095
00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:33.440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: had something to do with our lost bid to the UNSC,

asr-000096
00:18:34.120 --> 00:18:36.680
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: and to which you said in the affirmative,

asr-000097
00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:38.920
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ang gusto ko pong malaman nga,

asr-000098
00:18:39.400 --> 00:18:50.540
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ano po itong mga unresolved cases in the past administration that you think ay nakakapag-contribute doon sa paningin na iyon ng international community?

asr-000099
00:18:57.860 --> 00:19:02.240
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Madam Chair, Representative Montes,

asr-000100
00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:07.760
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: for example po, ang ating pong mga naka-accomplish po ay katulad po ng red tagging and EJA.

asr-000101
00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:13.240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay, thank you, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleagues.

asr-000102
00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:20.240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yung mga ganyan po, nabanggit niyo po yung mga red tagging EJK,

asr-000103
00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:22.380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: has the Commission

asr-000104
00:19:22.540 --> 00:19:23.160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: examined

asr-000105
00:19:23.240 --> 00:19:31.120
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Whether these concerns ng international community, consistent po ba yan sa findings ng Human Rights Commission?

asr-000106
00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:35.760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Po, ano po yung iniisip ng international community?

asr-000107
00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:39.680
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yan din po ba ang paningin ng CHR?

asr-000108
00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:41.460
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Yes po, Madam Chair.

asr-000109
00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:44.000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay po. Maraming salamat po.

asr-000110
00:19:46.800 --> 00:19:53.280
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Can CHR identify programs, especially in the 2027 budget

asr-000111
00:19:53.380 --> 00:20:00.740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: that have demonstrated measurable improvements in compliance with human rights standards?

asr-000112
00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:15.080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ano po yung mga programang nakapaloob dyan sa 2027 budget natin na magpapakita o magpapatunay na meron nga from the past administration, meron po tayong improvement ngayon?

asr-000113
00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:20.760
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: A human rights-centered national protection response mechanism.

asr-000114
00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:22.360
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: It integrates

asr-000115
00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:26.640
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: early warning, victim supports, and rapid response mechanism.

asr-000116
00:20:26.860 --> 00:20:32.640
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: So, meron po tayo ng mga tinatawag po nating programa, katulad po ng Bantay Karapatang Pantao,

asr-000117
00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:38.480
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: which detect, monitor, and prevent human rights risks through data and intelligence.

asr-000118
00:20:39.140 --> 00:20:46.320
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Kalinga Karapatang Pantao provides holistic, victim-centered support, protection, and recovery services.

asr-000119
00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:52.320
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: At syempre po, meron din po tayong Tugon Karapatang Pantao, which responds quickly, coordinates,

asr-000120
00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:55.980
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: intervention, and ensure protection and accountability.

asr-000121
00:20:56.500 --> 00:20:57.100
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Madam Chair.

asr-000122
00:20:57.620 --> 00:21:01.260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-000123
00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:04.640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Let me move on to my next question.

asr-000124
00:21:04.780 --> 00:21:10.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Just this morning, during the budget deliberations of the Dangerous Drugs Board,

asr-000125
00:21:11.300 --> 00:21:18.880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: the Sponsor, Congressman Marcy Cudoro, made mention of the necessity to include the Commission on Human Rights

asr-000126
00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:22.340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: as a part of the Board of the Dangerous Drugs Board.

asr-000127
00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:34.340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: If ever we include the CHR in the DDB, of course, by way of an amendment to the law creating the DDB,

asr-000128
00:21:34.340 --> 00:21:39.340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: how do you envision your role in shaping drug-related policy?

asr-000129
00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:48.340
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Madam Chair, alam niyo po, mandato po ng CHR, lahat po ng karapatang pantao ay lagi po natin ang gagampanan.

asr-000130
00:21:48.340 --> 00:21:52.300
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Pero doon po sa, kanina po sa Dangerous Drugs Board,

asr-000131
00:21:52.300 --> 00:21:58.640
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: siyempre po, more than willing po na makisama, makisuporta ang CHR,

asr-000132
00:21:59.020 --> 00:22:08.140
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: at magkaroon po kami ng sarili natin position paper sa lahat po ng mga cases na drug-related po.

asr-000133
00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:14.340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Actually, Madam Chair, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor,

asr-000134
00:22:14.340 --> 00:22:22.180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: what the DDB, what the sponsor of the DDB budget really wanted was to include the CHR

asr-000135
00:22:22.180 --> 00:22:33.640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: in the board as to help in formulating policies, kasi policymaking po yung Dangerous Drugs Board,

asr-000136
00:22:34.140 --> 00:22:36.320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: to help in the formulation of policies.

asr-000137
00:22:36.320 --> 00:22:43.960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, alam po natin naging issue yung mga EJK, mga drugs in the past.

asr-000138
00:22:44.620 --> 00:22:51.460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, I think it really is necessary to include the CHR there.

asr-000139
00:22:52.180 --> 00:23:02.780
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, halimbawa po, kasi I'm looking at, I'm willing to sponsor a bill tungkol po dyan.

asr-000140
00:23:02.780 --> 00:23:09.560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I'm looking at, for instance, in strengthening oversight sa human rights in drugs enforcement strategies.

asr-000141
00:23:09.740 --> 00:23:13.720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ano ang pwedeng maitulong ng CHR in that regard?

asr-000142
00:23:14.460 --> 00:23:18.900
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Okay. Sagutin ko po muna yung unang question nyo po ulit, Madam Chair.

asr-000143
00:23:19.480 --> 00:23:22.160
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: The DDB, no. The DDB has not included.

asr-000144
00:23:22.180 --> 00:23:27.240
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: The DDB has not engaged with CHR, but the CHR is more willing to be an observer po.

asr-000145
00:23:27.720 --> 00:23:35.300
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: With regards po sa drug-related po, CHR proposes that drug use to be treated as a public health issue.

asr-000146
00:23:35.900 --> 00:23:47.140
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Kasi po, drug use is currently being over-criminalized where users who need services to address their dependence or use are instead treated as criminals and jails.

asr-000147
00:23:47.140 --> 00:23:52.140
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Drug cases contribute to more than 70% of the jails.

asr-000148
00:23:52.180 --> 00:24:03.360
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: So, sa lahat po ng mga pinupuntahan po ng CHR, Madam Chair, 70% po ang mga nakakulong po sa ating mga PDLs po natin.

asr-000149
00:24:03.860 --> 00:24:09.040
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yeah. What you said was as observer. Is that correct? Did I hear you right?

asr-000150
00:24:09.300 --> 00:24:10.100
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Yes, Madam Chair.

asr-000151
00:24:11.300 --> 00:24:19.120
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Hindi po, hindi po sang-ayon na maging permanent seat sa board yung CHR.

asr-000152
00:24:19.120 --> 00:24:21.820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kasi kung ang pagbabasehan po natin,

asr-000153
00:24:22.180 --> 00:24:29.660
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: nung kung nga po una, kung naka-apekto yung mga EJK, mga problema ng human rights violations doon sa drugs,

asr-000154
00:24:30.080 --> 00:24:34.880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: hindi po ba dapat nandodon din ang CHR?

asr-000155
00:24:35.040 --> 00:24:41.920
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Kasi kung may mga usapin po tayo ng paglabag ng human rights doon sa mga biktima ng mga EJKs.

asr-000156
00:24:43.020 --> 00:24:49.780
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Madam Chair, ulitin po namin, we cannot because we have to maintain our independence po.

asr-000157
00:24:49.780 --> 00:24:51.100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay.

asr-000158
00:24:52.180 --> 00:24:59.780
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ibig sabihin po, kung sakasakali, your participation would only be limited to being an observer

asr-000159
00:24:59.780 --> 00:25:04.120
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: and not contributing to the policies of the Dangerous Drugs Board.

asr-000160
00:25:04.760 --> 00:25:12.960
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: We can contribute po. We can contribute po, Madam Chair, but we cannot sit as a regular member of the board, as an independent body.

asr-000161
00:25:13.680 --> 00:25:17.120
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: So, yan po yung mandato sa atin ng konstitusyon.

asr-000162
00:25:17.120 --> 00:25:21.380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Opo. Naiintindihan po natin yun, pero parte po din ng trabaho.

asr-000163
00:25:22.180 --> 00:25:28.720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Human rights ng CHR ang pagprotekta sa mga vulnerable grupo, katulad ng mga kabataan,

asr-000164
00:25:29.020 --> 00:25:35.140
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: and especially women, because the CHR has a gender—is the gender ombud.

asr-000165
00:25:35.560 --> 00:25:40.100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Now, these people, yung mga youth, yung mga women, sila usually ang nabibiktima.

asr-000166
00:25:41.480 --> 00:25:44.400
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ang karapatan nila ay nayuyurakan, natatapakan.

asr-000167
00:25:44.560 --> 00:25:47.880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, tungkulin ng CHR, then na maprotektahan sila.

asr-000168
00:25:47.880 --> 00:25:51.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, how do we reconcile now this mandate and this duty?

asr-000169
00:25:52.180 --> 00:25:55.260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: If you are saying na hindi yan mandato po ng CHR?

asr-000170
00:25:56.640 --> 00:26:03.180
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Madam Chair, kung Montes, I'm with you sa karapatan po ng lahat ng ating mga vulnerable sectors,

asr-000171
00:26:03.600 --> 00:26:12.320
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: but syempre po, CHR is not a part of the executive, but we can monitor and we are the advisor of the government.

asr-000172
00:26:13.580 --> 00:26:18.640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay, thank you so much, Madam Chair, distinguished sponsor.

asr-000173
00:26:18.640 --> 00:26:22.140
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ang sa akin lang po, it's also a matter of...

asr-000174
00:26:22.180 --> 00:26:25.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: you know, balancing security and rights in policymaking.

asr-000175
00:26:26.480 --> 00:26:30.380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: If the CHR does not see it that way,

asr-000176
00:26:30.860 --> 00:26:36.800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: then perhaps there are other ways for which CHR can be able to contribute to policies

asr-000177
00:26:36.800 --> 00:26:40.420
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: that affect human rights in the issue of drugs.

asr-000178
00:26:42.500 --> 00:26:44.840
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Madam Chair, Madam Speaker,

asr-000179
00:26:45.680 --> 00:26:50.500
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: CHR seats as observed in all interagency bodies,

asr-000180
00:26:50.740 --> 00:26:51.840
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: but it is also an activity...

asr-000181
00:26:52.180 --> 00:26:56.940
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: It is also an activity for which CHR can participate in awarding recommendations to different agencies.

asr-000182
00:26:57.400 --> 00:27:01.060
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: If that being so, Mr. Chair, kung nakaupo pala talaga doon,

asr-000183
00:27:01.580 --> 00:27:09.300
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ano po ang naging contribution ng CHR noong mga panahon na may mga aligasyon ng paglabag ng karapatang pantao

asr-000184
00:27:09.300 --> 00:27:16.800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: sa mga tokhang, sa mga EJ case, and all,

asr-000185
00:27:16.800 --> 00:27:21.800
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: na naging sanhi kung bakit napasama yung ating iman,

asr-000186
00:27:22.180 --> 00:27:24.100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: kahit sa international community.

asr-000187
00:27:31.780 --> 00:27:35.640
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: We are having our undertaking its own investigations.

asr-000188
00:27:36.200 --> 00:27:41.480
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: So lahat po ng cases na nagkakaroon po tayo being forwarded po sa CHR,

asr-000189
00:27:41.880 --> 00:27:43.920
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: unang-una po tinatanggap po natin yan.

asr-000190
00:27:44.340 --> 00:27:46.160
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Nagkakaroon po tayo ng investigation,

asr-000191
00:27:46.780 --> 00:27:49.800
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: at syempre po, hanggang doon lamang po ang ating mandato,

asr-000192
00:27:49.800 --> 00:27:51.520
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: we cannot file cases.

asr-000193
00:27:52.180 --> 00:27:56.920
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Pero we can endorse, recommend sa mga different agencies po.

asr-000194
00:27:57.980 --> 00:28:03.620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay. Maraming salamat po, Madam Chair, distinguished sponsor.

asr-000195
00:28:03.780 --> 00:28:05.640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Now let me move on.

asr-000196
00:28:06.140 --> 00:28:13.740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I was just exploring the possibility based on the pronouncements of Congressman Teodoro

asr-000197
00:28:13.740 --> 00:28:15.840
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: during the budget deliberation this morning.

asr-000198
00:28:16.540 --> 00:28:18.880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So let me move on to another topic.

asr-000199
00:28:20.020 --> 00:28:21.880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Recently, the CHR published...

asr-000200
00:28:22.180 --> 00:28:27.720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I would like to emphasize that it provides free information, education, and campaign or IEC materials

asr-000201
00:28:27.720 --> 00:28:31.000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: to individuals and organizations to promote human rights,

asr-000202
00:28:31.120 --> 00:28:35.200
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: particularly among vulnerable, marginalized, and disadvantaged sectors.

asr-000203
00:28:35.820 --> 00:28:40.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: May I ask the CHR, does the Commission specifically maintain IEC materials

asr-000204
00:28:40.700 --> 00:28:45.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: on the protection of women and violence, discrimination, harassment,

asr-000205
00:28:45.840 --> 00:28:47.820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: and other violations of human rights?

asr-000206
00:28:47.820 --> 00:28:49.700
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Madam Speaker, yes po.

asr-000207
00:28:50.260 --> 00:28:51.820
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Dire-direcho po ang ating...

asr-000208
00:28:52.180 --> 00:28:57.320
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: IEC materials information sa ating pong komisyon.

asr-000209
00:28:57.320 --> 00:29:02.740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Opo. Itong mga materials na ito, where do they exist?

asr-000210
00:29:02.740 --> 00:29:04.020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Online po ba?

asr-000211
00:29:04.020 --> 00:29:11.120
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: O are they distributed in far flung barangays, digital materials po lang ito?

asr-000212
00:29:11.120 --> 00:29:15.320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Because sa pagkakaalam ko po, parang online na, no?

asr-000213
00:29:15.320 --> 00:29:18.620
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: So, both physical and online po.

asr-000214
00:29:18.620 --> 00:29:20.120
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Available po yan.

asr-000215
00:29:20.120 --> 00:29:22.020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So may mga distribution din.

asr-000216
00:29:22.020 --> 00:29:22.820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Channels tayo.

asr-000217
00:29:22.880 --> 00:29:24.860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: How do we distribute it so that...

asr-000218
00:29:24.860 --> 00:29:26.500
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Yes po. Nagkakaroon po tayong...

asr-000219
00:29:26.500 --> 00:29:30.060
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Actually po, meron pong mga visitations sa various organizations,

asr-000220
00:29:30.800 --> 00:29:33.240
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: sa ating pong mga barangays, municipality,

asr-000221
00:29:33.900 --> 00:29:36.360
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: na umiikot po ang ating pong komisyon.

asr-000222
00:29:36.980 --> 00:29:37.760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Opo. Opo.

asr-000223
00:29:38.980 --> 00:29:43.480
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: How much po of your 2027 budget is allocated for the production,

asr-000224
00:29:44.320 --> 00:29:47.940
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: printing, and dissemination of these materials?

asr-000225
00:29:48.320 --> 00:29:49.040
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Magkano po?

asr-000226
00:29:50.660 --> 00:29:51.300
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ang...

asr-000227
00:29:51.300 --> 00:29:51.980
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Nakapaloob po.

asr-000228
00:29:52.020 --> 00:29:53.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Opo. Sa 2027 budget nila.

asr-000230
00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:09.820
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Madam Speaker, it's P94,643,000 ang aming proposed for 2027.

asr-000231
00:30:09.820 --> 00:30:15.580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Out of the P94,000,000, magkano ang halaga specifically targeting women?

asr-000232
00:30:17.420 --> 00:30:26.400
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Out of the P94,000,000, ilan po doon ang halagang specifically nakatarget sa production of materials for women po?

asr-000233
00:30:27.900 --> 00:30:29.240
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: For women?

asr-000234
00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:30.340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Opo.

asr-000235
00:30:32.540 --> 00:30:35.940
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Naka-lump sum po siya, Madam Speaker.

asr-000236
00:30:35.940 --> 00:30:43.580
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: So wala pong na-specific for women, for children; lump sum po siya para sa lahat po ng sectors.

asr-000237
00:30:43.940 --> 00:30:51.980
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Kasi nga po, Madam Speaker, medyo maliit po ang allocation po natin para sa buong Pilipinas po.

asr-000238
00:30:52.840 --> 00:30:55.200
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-000239
00:30:55.240 --> 00:30:59.640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: But I asked a while ago if there were materials specifically for,

asr-000240
00:30:59.640 --> 00:31:03.480
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: addressing violence against women, and meron po.

asr-000241
00:31:03.580 --> 00:31:07.380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So ibig sabihin po, ang nilalabas niyong materials, general na po yun.

asr-000242
00:31:07.720 --> 00:31:13.620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Walang specific IEC material na para lang sa, that addresses gender violence.

asr-000243
00:31:14.300 --> 00:31:14.840
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Meron po.

asr-000244
00:31:14.900 --> 00:31:15.720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Meron po.

asr-000245
00:31:16.080 --> 00:31:25.100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So out of this yun po sana ang gusto kong itanong, kung magkano, and ano na lang po siguro, doon sa allocation na yun,

asr-000246
00:31:25.660 --> 00:31:29.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ano po ang target natin na maabot ng mga kababaihan?

asr-000247
00:31:29.360 --> 00:31:34.680
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Half of our population, 50% is women, ano po.

asr-000248
00:31:34.860 --> 00:31:42.560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So ano po, maliit po ang budget ninyo, paano po natin maaabot o masasaklaw ang karamihan ng ating mga kababaihan?

asr-000249
00:31:42.860 --> 00:31:44.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Lalo na po yung mga nasa kanayunan.

asr-000250
00:31:46.220 --> 00:31:54.360
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Madam Speaker, ang aming pong GAD budget for 2027 ay 77 million pesos.

asr-000251
00:31:56.240 --> 00:31:57.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And doon po yun napupunta?

asr-000252
00:31:58.460 --> 00:31:58.940
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Yes po.

asr-000253
00:31:59.360 --> 00:31:59.600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay po.

asr-000254
00:31:59.960 --> 00:32:01.700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming maraming salamat po.

asr-000255
00:32:03.920 --> 00:32:12.020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Anyway, I still have a lot of questions but I committed to squeezing everything in.

asr-000256
00:32:12.020 --> 00:32:18.280
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So siguro, pang huli na lamang po, Madam Chair, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor,

asr-000257
00:32:18.660 --> 00:32:28.000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: nais ko na lamang pong ipahayag na ang kababaihan, kabalikatan para sa kapakanan at kaunlaran ng bayan o 4K

asr-000258
00:32:28.000 --> 00:32:29.020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ay kaisa ng human rights.

asr-000259
00:32:29.360 --> 00:32:39.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Commission on Human Rights na ipagtangkol at isulong ang karapatang pantao sa harap ng malaking hamon na tugunan ang mga problema ng human rights

asr-000260
00:32:39.360 --> 00:32:49.020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: sa ating bansa, nais din nating hikayatin ng CHR na palawakin ang saklaw ng kanilang trabaho, patibayin ang pagganap ng tungkulin

asr-000261
00:32:49.020 --> 00:32:57.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: at tiyakin na ang bawat pisong ipinagkakaloob ng taong bayan ay tinutumbasan ng pananagutan at kongkretong resulta.

asr-000262
00:32:57.360 --> 00:32:59.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Sa ganitong paraan,

asr-000263
00:32:59.360 --> 00:33:05.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: maipapakita natin na ang pondo ay tunay na giging proteksyon at katarungan para sa mamamayan.

asr-000264
00:33:06.300 --> 00:33:12.100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po, Madam Chair, Distinguished Sponsor. Magandang gabi po sa inyong lahat.

asr-000265
00:33:12.840 --> 00:33:13.640
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: [unclear] Leader.

asr-000266
00:33:24.040 --> 00:33:29.340
Rep. Manuel "Wowo" L. Fortes Jr.: Madam Speaker, I move that we recognize Representative Antonio L.

asr-000267
00:33:29.340 --> 00:33:32.160
Rep. Manuel "Wowo" L. Fortes Jr.: Tinio of ACT Teacher Partylist.

asr-000268
00:33:32.840 --> 00:33:38.860
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Representative Antonio Tinio of ACT Teacher Partylist is hereby recognized for his interpellation.

asr-000269
00:33:40.580 --> 00:33:42.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Salamat po, Madam Speaker.

asr-000270
00:33:43.180 --> 00:33:57.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Madam Speaker, ang tanong ko po ay kaugnay sa drug war, sa drug war ng nakaraang administrasyon ni dating Pangulong Duterte.

asr-000271
00:33:57.260 --> 00:33:59.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung extrajudicial killing.

asr-000272
00:33:59.360 --> 00:34:07.420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At yung pagpaslang ng libu-libong mga kababayan nating Pilipino.

asr-000273
00:34:09.140 --> 00:34:17.920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Isang malaking tagumpay po para sa naghahangad ng justisya, sa mga naghahangad ng justisya sa ating lipunan,

asr-000274
00:34:18.920 --> 00:34:24.460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sa mga biktima ng extrajudicial killing sa kanilang mga pamilyang naiwan,

asr-000275
00:34:24.460 --> 00:34:28.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang pagkaka-aresto.

asr-000276
00:34:29.360 --> 00:34:38.840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At paglilitis kay dating Pangulong Duterte sa International Criminal Court.

asr-000277
00:34:38.840 --> 00:34:40.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So mahalagang tagumpay po yun.

asr-000278
00:34:41.620 --> 00:34:50.300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At alam natin, hindi natatapos ang pagpapanagot kay Pangulong Duterte.

asr-000279
00:34:50.440 --> 00:34:57.640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bagaman siya ang, tama lang, siya bilang Pangulo, siya ang pinakamalaking isda.

asr-000280
00:34:57.640 --> 00:34:58.640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa...

asr-000281
00:34:59.360 --> 00:35:03.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: nag-anap na crimes against humanity.

asr-000282
00:35:05.080 --> 00:35:12.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Alam din natin na yung ICC nag-issue na ng warrant laban sa kanyang kanang kamay.

asr-000283
00:35:14.080 --> 00:35:20.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung dati niyang PNP chief naging senador, ngayon ay nagtatago sa warrant,

asr-000284
00:35:20.280 --> 00:35:26.500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sen. Bato de la Rosa, at sinasabi na mayroon pang ibang mga warrant na may issue.

asr-000285
00:35:28.060 --> 00:35:29.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero alam din natin,

asr-000286
00:35:29.360 --> 00:35:40.360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: na yung accountability para sa mga pagpaslang na iyan ay hindi limitado sa mga nasa pinakataas.

asr-000287
00:35:41.940 --> 00:35:51.960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung chain of command at yung dugo ng extrajudicial killings ay mula sa taas,

asr-000288
00:35:52.180 --> 00:35:57.740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: dadalo yan sa hanggang sa panggitna, sa antas na panggitna hanggang sa pinakababa.

asr-000289
00:35:58.480 --> 00:35:58.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

asr-000290
00:35:59.360 --> 00:36:05.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa mga aktual na mga opisyal at rank and file ng PNP, among others,

asr-000291
00:36:06.500 --> 00:36:08.060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: na aktual na nagpatupad,

asr-000292
00:36:08.680 --> 00:36:09.900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: nung mga inutos sa taas,

asr-000293
00:36:10.640 --> 00:36:12.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: yung aktual na mga pumatay.

asr-000294
00:36:12.220 --> 00:36:25.540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So kaya po napakahalaga na sa loob ng ating bansa at sa pangunguna ng ating mga institusyon

asr-000295
00:36:25.540 --> 00:36:28.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ay magpatuloy ang trabaho na...

asr-000296
00:36:29.360 --> 00:36:37.860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ng pag-iimbestiga at pagpapanagot sa lahat ng naging sangkot sa extrajudicial killings

asr-000297
00:36:37.860 --> 00:36:39.960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sa ngalan ng peking drug war na ito.

asr-000298
00:36:40.760 --> 00:36:40.920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-000299
00:36:40.920 --> 00:36:50.940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kaugnay nun ng ang isa sa mga institusyon na inaasahan natin na magsagawa at magtuloy

asr-000300
00:36:50.940 --> 00:36:57.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sa napakahalagang gawaing ito ay ang Commission on Human Rights.

asr-000301
00:36:58.280 --> 00:36:58.920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No? At...

asr-000302
00:36:59.360 --> 00:37:12.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Last year ay nagpahayag ang Commission on Human Rights na nagbukas sila ng imbestigasyon,

asr-000303
00:37:12.500 --> 00:37:22.500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: review and investigation of several hundred mga cases of drug war killings.

asr-000304
00:37:23.760 --> 00:37:27.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pwede po bang for the record ay mabanggit lang

asr-000305
00:37:27.600 --> 00:37:28.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ilan po yung mga...

asr-000308
00:37:29.360 --> 00:37:36.820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: kabuo ang kaso na sinimulang investigahan muli ng Commission on Human Rights?

asr-000309
00:37:40.740 --> 00:37:50.400
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Madam Speaker, in particular, the Commission has identified 493 cases for reinvestigation in 2024

asr-000310
00:37:50.400 --> 00:37:58.080
