asr-001226
01:51:33.720 --> 01:52:17.080
Rep. Jonathan Keith T. Flores: Undersecretary Christian Mark Guingcangco; Assistant Secretary Melvyn Carlo Barroa; Assistant Secretary Ryan Martin [unclear]; Assistant Secretary Maria Victoria Castro; Assistant Secretary Celine Melanie Dee; Assistant Secretary Pinky Jimenez; and Assistant Secretary Emmy Lou Versoza-Delfin.

asr-001227
01:52:17.080 --> 01:52:49.280
Rep. Jonathan Keith T. Flores: Likewise representing the Cybercrime Investigation and Coordinating Center, Executive Director Renato Paraiso; the National Privacy Commission, Privacy Commissioner and Chairman Johann Carlos Barcena; and the National Telecommunications Commission, Commissioner Ella Blanca Lopez.

asr-001227-split-2
01:52:49.280 --> 01:52:59.160
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: We acknowledge the presence of the heads and officials of DICT and its attached agencies. Welcome to the House of Representatives.

asr-001228
01:52:59.160 --> 01:53:10.110
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: And with regard to the motion of the Majority Leader, is there any objection? The Chair hears none. The motion is approved. Majority Leader.

asr-001229
01:53:10.120 --> 01:53:38.080
Rep. Jonathan Keith T. Flores: I move, Madam Speaker, that we recognize Vice Chair Brian Poe, the vice chairperson of the Committee on Appropriations, to sponsor the proposed budget of the Department of Information and Communications Technology and its attached agencies.

asr-001230
01:53:38.080 --> 01:54:02.000
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Is there any objection? The Chair hears none. Representative Vice Chair Brian Poe, [unclear]. Of course, the vice chairman of the Committee on Appropriations is hereby recognized to begin the sponsorship of the budget of DICT and its attached agencies. Vice Chair may now proceed with his sponsorship speech.

asr-001231
01:54:02.000 --> 01:54:38.320
Rep. Brian Poe: Thank you, Madam Speaker. I happily address my colleagues here in plenary. I rise to sponsor the proposed fiscal year 2027 budget of the Department of Information and Communications Technology and its attached agencies. For fiscal year 2027, DICT and its attached agencies are proposing a total expenditure program of 19.49 billion pesos, an increase of 1.27 billion, or 7%, from fiscal year 2026.

asr-001232
01:54:38.320 --> 01:55:04.880
Rep. Brian Poe: A significant portion of this budget goes to ICT infrastructure. The ICT Systems and Information Infrastructure Program receives 3.85 billion, as well as 1.13 billion for the National Broadband Plan, up by 69.3%, and 949.5 million for the National Government Data Center, up 27%.

asr-001233
01:55:04.880 --> 01:55:32.160
Rep. Brian Poe: These investments are already producing results. The National Fiber Backbone has laid 3,026 kilometers of fiber; 59 of 136 backbone nodes have been activated. And the Philippine Digital Infrastructure Project has an estimated cost of 16.1 billion, with 2.16 billion programmed for fiscal year 2027.

asr-001234
01:55:32.160 --> 01:56:00.550
Rep. Brian Poe: For connectivity, DICT reported 29,091 active free Wi-Fi points across 11,839—sorry, I stand corrected—11,836 locations as of July 2026. The Free Public Internet Access Program has 5 billion pesos in automatic appropriations for fiscal year 2027.

asr-001235
01:56:00.560 --> 01:56:10.830
Rep. Brian Poe: Our digital government infrastructure is also operating at a significant scale. The eGov PH application has surpassed 61 million downloads

asr-001245
01:56:10.840 --> 01:56:19.070
Rep. Brian Poe: and 56 million verified accounts, while eGov DX has

asr-001255
01:56:19.080 --> 01:56:30.000
Rep. Brian Poe: processed more than 1.2 billion transactions and integrated over 1,300 government e-services.

asr-001264
01:56:30.000 --> 01:56:48.760
Rep. Brian Poe: Cybersecurity, the National Security Operations Center, has expanded its coverage from 10 government agencies in 2022 to 99 agencies as of August 2026, monitoring approximately 6.7 billion security alerts.

asr-001265
01:56:48.760 --> 01:57:09.260
Rep. Brian Poe: But as we support these investments, we must also look closely at implementation. DICT's fiscal year 2025 obligation rate was 61.7%, leaving approximately 9.16 billion in unused appropriations.

asr-001266
01:57:09.260 --> 01:57:18.260
Rep. Brian Poe: For the ICT Systems and Information Infrastructure Program, obligation was 43.5%. Disbursement was 22.6%.

asr-001267
01:57:18.760 --> 01:57:27.360
Rep. Brian Poe: These figures remind us that the measure of budget is not only what we appropriate, but what is actually delivered.

asr-001268
01:57:27.880 --> 01:57:41.860
Rep. Brian Poe: And while we recognize the progress made, we also recognize that there are many shortcomings still, not only in cybersecurity, but also in combating fake news and other areas of digital safety and governance.

asr-001269
01:57:41.860 --> 01:57:46.740
Rep. Brian Poe: These are challenges that will require continued work and scrutiny.

asr-001273
01:57:48.860 --> 01:57:57.680
Rep. Brian Poe: And while many may look at it as an opportunity to reduce funding for the agency, I see this as a challenge to increase funding where it is critically necessary.

asr-001274
01:57:57.680 --> 01:58:10.000
Rep. Brian Poe: These programs are of the utmost importance for the development of our country in this new age of innovation, AI, cybersecurity, and other threats.

asr-001275
01:58:10.560 --> 01:58:16.360
Rep. Brian Poe: So, Madam Speaker, with that, we are ready to take the questions of our distinguished colleagues, and I thank you.

asr-001276
01:58:16.360 --> 01:58:18.420
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Majority Leader.

asr-001277
01:58:21.740 --> 01:58:37.700
Rep. Jonathan Keith T. Flores: Madam Speaker, I move that we recognize the Honorable Robert Nazal of BH Party-list to interpellate on the proposed budget.

asr-001278
01:58:38.640 --> 01:58:43.460
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Representative Robert Nazal of BH Party-list is hereby recognized for his interpellation.

asr-001279
01:58:44.200 --> 01:58:45.720
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Good evening, Madam Chair.

asr-001280
01:58:46.360 --> 01:58:49.600
Rep. Brian Poe: Good evening to my distinguished colleague.

asr-001281
01:58:50.060 --> 01:58:50.420
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Good evening.

asr-001282
01:58:51.120 --> 01:58:52.700
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And good evening to the DICT.

asr-001283
01:58:54.420 --> 01:59:04.320
Rep. Roberto Nazal: On the mandate of DICT, distinguished colleague, Mr. Sponsor, Madam Chair, I want to start with DICT's mandate.

asr-001284
01:59:06.160 --> 01:59:09.400
Rep. Roberto Nazal: DICT is supposed to lead our national ICT agenda.

asr-001285
01:59:09.400 --> 01:59:14.400
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And under Republic Act 12254,

asr-001286
01:59:16.360 --> 01:59:23.200
Rep. Roberto Nazal: we have an even bigger responsibility for whole of government digitalization and interoperability.

asr-001287
01:59:26.020 --> 01:59:32.780
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Chair, distinguished colleague, Mr. Secretary, are you actually fulfilling that mandate?

asr-001288
01:59:34.100 --> 01:59:34.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And how?

asr-001289
01:59:36.160 --> 01:59:39.520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Because DICT should be more than Wi-Fi and connectivity.

asr-001290
01:59:40.480 --> 01:59:45.520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: You should also make sure that government uses technology efficiently.

asr-001291
01:59:46.360 --> 01:59:51.120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: For example, are we oversubscribed in cloud services?

asr-001292
01:59:52.640 --> 01:59:56.100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Do you know how much cloud capacity government is paying?

asr-001293
01:59:57.100 --> 01:59:59.980
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Paying for versus actual average and peak?

asr-001294
02:00:00.000 --> 02:00:09.000
Rep. Roberto Nazal: What about internet services? Are we paying for more bandwidth than government actually uses?

asr-001295
02:00:11.000 --> 02:00:24.460
Rep. Roberto Nazal: During our previous hearing, you told us Republic Act 12254 could save government at least 30% by eliminating repetitive common systems and subscriptions.

asr-001296
02:00:24.460 --> 02:00:33.300
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Have you already identified these duplications? How much can government actually save? And when will we see those savings?

asr-001297
02:00:35.540 --> 02:00:44.380
Rep. Brian Poe: Thank you, Madam Speaker. Those are very valid questions from my colleague. Let's go through it one by one very quickly.

asr-001298
02:00:44.380 --> 02:00:54.300
Rep. Brian Poe: So yes, Madam Speaker, DICT is implementing its mandate beyond the connectivity and moving towards a whole of government.

asr-001299
02:00:54.460 --> 02:01:06.280
Rep. Brian Poe: And that is currently being implemented through the DICT and its attached agencies.

asr-001300
02:01:06.280 --> 02:01:16.080
Rep. Brian Poe: For fiscal year 2027 alone, the department targets integration of 40 agencies with the Citizen Frontline Delivery Services Platform,

asr-001301
02:01:16.560 --> 02:01:24.440
Rep. Brian Poe: 30 agencies, each of which with HCMIS and IFMIS, and 30 agencies with OFMIS.

asr-001302
02:01:24.460 --> 02:01:27.620
Rep. Brian Poe: And that includes the Online Public Service Portal and Procurement Systems.

asr-001303
02:01:28.280 --> 02:01:34.100
Rep. Brian Poe: Regarding the concern on cloud and bandwidth and other common ICT requirements,

asr-001304
02:01:34.280 --> 02:01:42.100
Rep. Brian Poe: the objective of e-Government Act is precisely to give government greater visibility over what common requirements exist

asr-001305
02:01:42.100 --> 02:01:46.080
Rep. Brian Poe: and to avoid paying repeatedly for the same capabilities.

asr-001306
02:01:46.080 --> 02:01:54.080
Rep. Brian Poe: So the management mechanism that we have here, and its ability to validate across

asr-001307
02:01:54.460 --> 02:01:59.460
Rep. Brian Poe: 450 national agencies for compliance, is established within the eGov portfolio.

asr-001308
02:01:59.460 --> 02:02:10.580
Rep. Brian Poe: But we should not complain or I mean we should not claim, sorry, rather, that DICT is oversubscribed in terms of its cloud or bandwidth

asr-001309
02:02:10.580 --> 02:02:18.880
Rep. Brian Poe: because the submissions presently available to DICT do not yet establish government-wide average and peak utilization

asr-001310
02:02:18.880 --> 02:02:22.580
Rep. Brian Poe: across or against total contracted capacity.

asr-001311
02:02:22.580 --> 02:02:24.080
Rep. Brian Poe: So with that, we can...

asr-001312
02:02:24.460 --> 02:02:29.500
Rep. Brian Poe: We can commit to Congress to establish that a baseline through the inventory, portfolio management,

asr-001313
02:02:29.920 --> 02:02:36.020
Rep. Brian Poe: and interoperability mechanisms are being implemented under RA 12254.

asr-001314
02:02:36.380 --> 02:02:42.800
Rep. Brian Poe: The 30% figure that my colleague brought up, Madam Speaker, is a very valid number to bring up

asr-001315
02:02:42.800 --> 02:02:44.840
Rep. Brian Poe: because we did make that commitment.

asr-001316
02:02:45.320 --> 02:02:51.540
Rep. Brian Poe: And the figure, therefore, should be treated at this stage as a potential cost avoidance estimate

asr-001317
02:02:52.340 --> 02:02:53.540
Rep. Brian Poe: from eliminating duplicative...

asr-001318
02:02:54.460 --> 02:03:00.480
Rep. Brian Poe: ...common systems and subscriptions, not yet as realized savings.

asr-001319
02:03:00.920 --> 02:03:03.320
Rep. Brian Poe: So really, this is the target that we hope to hit.

asr-001320
02:03:04.540 --> 02:03:08.980
Rep. Brian Poe: And yes, as of the last committee hearing that we had, Madam Speaker,

asr-001321
02:03:09.380 --> 02:03:15.300
Rep. Brian Poe: I do remember that the DICT is actively identifying where those duplications exist

asr-001322
02:03:15.300 --> 02:03:22.160
Rep. Brian Poe: and we're progressively moving towards a consolidated system, common ICT investments,

asr-001323
02:03:22.160 --> 02:03:23.920
Rep. Brian Poe: as agencies transition.

asr-001324
02:03:24.460 --> 02:03:32.440
Rep. Brian Poe: So I believe that we're really targeting that by the end of this administration,

asr-001325
02:03:32.440 --> 02:03:36.500
Rep. Brian Poe: we have a more centralized EGov system.

asr-001326
02:03:37.840 --> 02:03:39.880
Rep. Brian Poe: I hope that answers my colleague's questions.

asr-001327
02:03:39.880 --> 02:03:42.100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you for that, Distinguished Sponsor, Madam Chair.

asr-001328
02:03:42.720 --> 02:03:49.140
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Do we already have a number on the target in terms of the 30% savings that we will generate?

asr-001329
02:03:49.620 --> 02:03:51.120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Do we already have a figure?

asr-001330
02:03:52.060 --> 02:03:53.440
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, may I clarify?

asr-001331
02:03:53.660 --> 02:03:54.440
Rep. Brian Poe: A number on how much?

asr-001332
02:03:54.440 --> 02:03:55.680
Rep. Brian Poe: How much has been saved already?

asr-001333
02:03:55.900 --> 02:03:56.180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Yes.

asr-001334
02:03:56.640 --> 02:03:58.960
Rep. Brian Poe: Let me get back to you on that.

asr-001335
02:04:01.640 --> 02:04:08.620
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, the DICT's claim is that they don't have a set number yet,

asr-001336
02:04:09.000 --> 02:04:11.220
Rep. Brian Poe: although they are studying it.

asr-001337
02:04:11.800 --> 02:04:15.520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Is there a target number in terms of savings?

asr-001338
02:04:16.100 --> 02:04:19.320
Rep. Brian Poe: For this year or for fiscal year 2027?

asr-001339
02:04:19.680 --> 02:04:20.920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: For this year.

asr-001340
02:04:21.260 --> 02:04:21.720
Rep. Roberto Nazal: For this year.

asr-001341
02:04:21.720 --> 02:04:22.740
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And fiscal year 2027.

asr-001342
02:04:24.440 --> 02:04:34.700
Rep. Brian Poe: But that's for this.

asr-001343
02:04:35.700 --> 02:04:38.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: But for this year, we'll allow it.

asr-001344
02:04:38.840 --> 02:04:39.120
Rep. Brian Poe: Okay.

asr-001345
02:04:39.520 --> 02:04:42.900
Rep. Brian Poe: Because this is a new law, a newly passed law,

asr-001346
02:04:43.360 --> 02:04:47.720
Rep. Brian Poe: the actual estimated savings are for fiscal year 2027,

asr-001347
02:04:47.720 --> 02:04:52.720
Rep. Brian Poe: and we're looking at, if I'm not mistaken, 15 billion pesos in estimated savings

asr-001348
02:04:53.400 --> 02:04:53.720
Rep. Brian Poe: by removing

asr-001349
02:04:53.720 --> 02:04:55.360
Rep. Brian Poe: By removing these duplications.

asr-001350
02:04:56.900 --> 02:05:04.020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Are we also looking at using AI to monitor all these systems?

asr-001351
02:05:04.020 --> 02:05:05.020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So that...

asr-001352
02:05:05.840 --> 02:05:11.160
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, DICT can confirm that we are using AI.

asr-001353
02:05:12.140 --> 02:05:14.540
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you for that, Distinguished Sponsor, Madam Speaker.

asr-001354
02:05:15.860 --> 02:05:17.820
Rep. Roberto Nazal: I'll go to my next question.

asr-001355
02:05:18.680 --> 02:05:21.860
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Chair, Madam Speaker, during the previous hearing,

asr-001356
02:05:21.860 --> 02:05:29.120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Distinguished Sponsor, I also raised that the DICT has a 9% obligation rate.

asr-001357
02:05:29.880 --> 02:05:33.360
Rep. Roberto Nazal: We are told now that this has improved to around 27%.

asr-001358
02:05:33.360 --> 02:05:35.200
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Is this correct?

asr-001359
02:05:36.340 --> 02:05:39.860
Rep. Brian Poe: Yes, Madam Speaker, I can confirm we've increased to 27%.

asr-001360
02:05:40.620 --> 02:05:43.200
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, okay naman po na hindi na 9%.

asr-001361
02:05:43.200 --> 02:05:49.960
Rep. Roberto Nazal: 27% na, pero I hope we shouldn't be happy with this, no?

asr-001362
02:05:50.440 --> 02:05:51.540
Rep. Roberto Nazal: This is still very low.

asr-001363
02:05:51.860 --> 02:05:58.800
Rep. Roberto Nazal: May I ask, why, what is stopping us from improving on the 27%?

asr-001364
02:05:59.400 --> 02:06:00.420
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Ano ba ang problema natin?

asr-001365
02:06:00.580 --> 02:06:03.120
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, I completely agree with my colleague.

asr-001366
02:06:03.280 --> 02:06:05.440
Rep. Brian Poe: 27% is not something to celebrate,

asr-001367
02:06:05.700 --> 02:06:08.600
Rep. Brian Poe: especially when there are so many other agencies that need funding.

asr-001368
02:06:09.280 --> 02:06:10.760
Rep. Brian Poe: But it is an improvement.

asr-001369
02:06:10.980 --> 02:06:14.540
Rep. Brian Poe: And I'll list down the things that are making it difficult.

asr-001370
02:06:15.120 --> 02:06:16.840
Rep. Brian Poe: One is procurement delays.

asr-001371
02:06:16.840 --> 02:06:21.840
Rep. Brian Poe: Two is the technical complexity of what DICT's management,

asr-001372
02:06:21.860 --> 02:06:23.880
Rep. Brian Poe: mandate, puts them in charge of.

asr-001373
02:06:24.200 --> 02:06:26.620
Rep. Brian Poe: Three is the timing of the release of funds.

asr-001374
02:06:27.100 --> 02:06:30.360
Rep. Brian Poe: Many of the releases were quite late this year for DICT.

asr-001375
02:06:30.820 --> 02:06:34.860
Rep. Brian Poe: And so, many of the funds are just now being released.

asr-001376
02:06:35.320 --> 02:06:38.360
Rep. Brian Poe: We also have a limited specialized manpower.

asr-001377
02:06:38.800 --> 02:06:45.420
Rep. Brian Poe: Unlike many other agencies, DICT requires a lot of specialized manpower, Madam Speaker.

asr-001378
02:06:45.420 --> 02:06:50.780
Rep. Brian Poe: And with that, we actually do need to increase the manpower of the agency

asr-001379
02:06:50.780 --> 02:06:51.620
Rep. Brian Poe: in order to...

asr-001380
02:06:51.860 --> 02:06:56.460
Rep. Brian Poe: ...increase its absorptive capacity and the services it provides.

asr-001381
02:06:56.460 --> 02:07:05.360
Rep. Brian Poe: Lastly, PDIP had two unsuccessful biddings and had to restructure its major procurement package.

asr-001382
02:07:05.360 --> 02:07:09.360
Rep. Brian Poe: And all of that combined leads to 27%.

asr-001383
02:07:09.360 --> 02:07:15.220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: What obligation rate, Mr. Sponsor, are we looking at for December 31?

asr-001384
02:07:21.860 --> 02:07:38.360
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, the agency is optimistically pointing out that we're looking at 90% completion by December.

asr-001385
02:07:38.900 --> 02:07:46.440
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, are we saying that considering what you've mentioned, Madam Chair and Mr. Sponsor,

asr-001386
02:07:47.540 --> 02:07:50.120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: maaayos na po natin yung procurement issues,

asr-001387
02:07:50.900 --> 02:07:51.720
Rep. Roberto Nazal: all the funnels,

asr-001388
02:07:51.860 --> 02:07:53.900
Rep. Roberto Nazal: kung saan po tayo nagkaka-roadblock?

asr-001389
02:07:54.600 --> 02:07:56.520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: In terms of technical manpower,

asr-001390
02:07:57.200 --> 02:08:00.020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: we will have all the technical manpower prior to that?

asr-001391
02:08:03.300 --> 02:08:06.460
Rep. Brian Poe: Just to clarify the target,

asr-001392
02:08:06.600 --> 02:08:08.940
Rep. Brian Poe: as of today, we're at 35% already.

asr-001393
02:08:09.420 --> 02:08:09.980
Rep. Brian Poe: As of today.

asr-001394
02:08:11.240 --> 02:08:13.120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And we are expecting how much? 90?

asr-001395
02:08:13.840 --> 02:08:14.320
Rep. Brian Poe: 90%.

asr-001396
02:08:14.320 --> 02:08:16.640
Rep. Brian Poe: And if you think about it,

asr-001397
02:08:16.660 --> 02:08:18.480
Rep. Brian Poe: when we had the initial data to today,

asr-001398
02:08:18.480 --> 02:08:21.480
Rep. Brian Poe: we already moved up 9%.

asr-001399
02:08:21.860 --> 02:08:23.000
Rep. Brian Poe: More or less.

asr-001400
02:08:23.480 --> 02:08:24.780
Rep. Brian Poe: If we continue at this rate,

asr-001401
02:08:24.860 --> 02:08:27.200
Rep. Brian Poe: we could possibly hit our target of 90%.

asr-001402
02:08:27.200 --> 02:08:30.720
Rep. Brian Poe: One of the things that the agency had to deal with

asr-001403
02:08:30.720 --> 02:08:33.920
Rep. Brian Poe: was really just waiting for the download of funding.

asr-001404
02:08:34.920 --> 02:08:38.420
Rep. Brian Poe: And so, there was time to already streamline some of the processes

asr-001405
02:08:38.420 --> 02:08:41.940
Rep. Brian Poe: for the release of these funds and the activation on the ground.

asr-001406
02:08:42.180 --> 02:08:45.280
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, what you're saying, Distinguished Sponsor, Madam Speaker,

asr-001407
02:08:46.040 --> 02:08:50.360
Rep. Roberto Nazal: is that maayos na po tayo in terms of the procurement process

asr-001408
02:08:50.360 --> 02:08:51.840
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and all the technical manpower.

asr-001409
02:08:51.860 --> 02:08:55.640
Rep. Roberto Nazal: But our main problem right now is the DBM.

asr-001410
02:08:56.700 --> 02:09:01.120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And how long, and kailan natin natatanggap yung pera?

asr-001411
02:09:01.940 --> 02:09:02.480
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Is this correct?

asr-001412
02:09:10.540 --> 02:09:14.880
Rep. Brian Poe: The reason why is not necessarily DBM.

asr-001413
02:09:15.180 --> 02:09:17.860
Rep. Brian Poe: It turns out it's because the awarding of major projects

asr-001414
02:09:17.860 --> 02:09:20.860
Rep. Brian Poe: to the DICT

asr-001415
02:09:21.860 --> 02:09:23.260
Rep. Brian Poe: will take place within this quarter.

asr-001416
02:09:23.940 --> 02:09:25.580
Rep. Brian Poe: So, once those have been awarded already,

asr-001417
02:09:25.800 --> 02:09:27.320
Rep. Brian Poe: that would be immediately dispersed.

asr-001418
02:09:27.500 --> 02:09:30.560
Rep. Brian Poe: But that doesn't necessarily have anything to do with the DBM.

asr-001419
02:09:30.980 --> 02:09:34.440
Rep. Roberto Nazal: When were these projects supposed to be procured?

asr-001420
02:09:35.580 --> 02:09:36.940
Rep. Roberto Nazal: When did they start?

asr-001421
02:09:49.900 --> 02:09:51.020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: But when did it start?

asr-001422
02:09:51.860 --> 02:10:06.400
Rep. Brian Poe: At the start of the year

asr-001426
02:10:14.060 --> 02:10:20.140
Rep. Brian Poe: So, PDIP, which constitutes 4 billion pesos, Madam Speaker,

asr-001427
02:10:20.140 --> 02:10:21.260
Rep. Brian Poe: is a big chunk of it.

asr-001428
02:10:21.260 --> 02:10:22.920
Rep. Brian Poe: And the reason why it was delayed

asr-001429
02:10:22.920 --> 02:10:25.640
Rep. Brian Poe: was because earlier this year, dear colleague,

asr-001430
02:10:26.160 --> 02:10:27.540
Rep. Brian Poe: they actually had a failed bidding.

asr-001431
02:10:28.240 --> 02:10:31.660
Rep. Brian Poe: So, now it's proceeding, but it's proceeding in October.

asr-001432
02:10:32.340 --> 02:10:35.380
Rep. Brian Poe: So, that's why the 4 billion will be released quite later.

asr-001433
02:10:35.400 --> 02:10:38.180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: But this was a project procurement for 2026 or 2025?

asr-001434
02:10:40.320 --> 02:10:43.460
Rep. Brian Poe: It's a continuing from 2025 to 2026.

asr-001435
02:10:44.380 --> 02:10:44.980
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Okay.

asr-001436
02:10:45.600 --> 02:10:48.000
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Let me go to my next question.

asr-001437
02:10:48.000 --> 02:10:49.940
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Having said that,

asr-001438
02:10:50.420 --> 02:10:51.240
Rep. Roberto Nazal: DICT's

asr-001439
02:10:51.260 --> 02:10:54.200
Rep. Roberto Nazal: absorptive capacity remains a problem,

asr-001440
02:10:54.880 --> 02:10:57.380
Rep. Roberto Nazal: I also want to be fair to the agency.

asr-001441
02:10:58.320 --> 02:11:02.960
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Hindi lahat ng hindi nababayaran ay necessarily Absorptive Capacity problem.

asr-001442
02:11:04.180 --> 02:11:07.360
Rep. Roberto Nazal: DICT's September 15 submission says

asr-001443
02:11:07.720 --> 02:11:09.720
Rep. Roberto Nazal: that as of August 31,

asr-001444
02:11:10.320 --> 02:11:15.800
Rep. Roberto Nazal: you had approximately 1.29 billion in accounts payable.

asr-001445
02:11:16.200 --> 02:11:21.060
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Of that, approximately 1.049 billion pertains to

asr-001446
02:11:21.060 --> 02:11:26.560
Rep. Roberto Nazal: valid and duly supported obligations from 2024 and 2025

asr-001447
02:11:26.560 --> 02:11:29.560
Rep. Roberto Nazal: that are already due and demandable.

asr-001448
02:11:30.560 --> 02:11:36.060
Rep. Roberto Nazal: You also say additional NCA from DBM is needed to settle these obligations.

asr-001449
02:11:36.660 --> 02:11:40.060
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, for this 1.049 billion,

asr-001450
02:11:40.560 --> 02:11:44.660
Rep. Roberto Nazal: is the problem now lack of cash authority from DBM

asr-001451
02:11:44.860 --> 02:11:47.460
Rep. Roberto Nazal: rather than lack of appropriation?

asr-001452
02:11:51.060 --> 02:12:04.260
Rep. Roberto Nazal: How much additional NCA do you need today to settle all valid, due, and demandable obligations?

asr-001454
02:12:07.720 --> 02:12:20.620
Rep. Brian Poe: Yes, I can confirm that there is a payable of 1.049 billion and this, actually, we do need an additional allocation.

asr-001455
02:12:20.620 --> 02:12:22.620
Rep. Brian Poe: In order to pay for.

asr-001456
02:12:24.620 --> 02:12:29.620
Rep. Brian Poe: And these are considered as milestone payments, Madam Speaker.

asr-001457
02:12:32.620 --> 02:12:36.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, Madam Chair, Madam Speaker,

asr-001458
02:12:38.620 --> 02:12:43.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: if these are already valid, duly supported, and due and demandable obligations,

asr-001459
02:12:43.620 --> 02:12:46.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and DICT submits the complete requirements,

asr-001460
02:12:46.620 --> 02:12:49.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: ang assumption po natin dito is complete na yung requirements nito.

asr-001461
02:12:50.620 --> 02:12:51.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Everything is complete.

asr-001462
02:12:54.620 --> 02:13:01.620
Rep. Brian Poe: So, Madam Speaker, I can confirm that all the requirements needed to request for additional funding for NCA from DBM

asr-001463
02:13:01.620 --> 02:13:05.620
Rep. Brian Poe: is complete and it's actually subject for approval already.

asr-001464
02:13:06.620 --> 02:13:07.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, what is the reason?

asr-001465
02:13:08.620 --> 02:13:14.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: What are they saying is the reason why hindi pa ito nababayaran?

asr-001466
02:13:14.620 --> 02:13:15.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Bakit po?

asr-001467
02:13:15.620 --> 02:13:17.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: What is the reason for the delay?

asr-001468
02:13:18.620 --> 02:13:19.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Why is there no NCA?

asr-001479
02:13:45.500 --> 02:13:46.600
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Could you pause my time, please?

asr-001480
02:13:48.100 --> 02:13:48.400
Rep. Brian Poe: Okay.

asr-001481
02:13:48.620 --> 02:13:56.860
Rep. Brian Poe: The documents were submitted first semester of this year—sorry, third quarter of this year, dear colleague.

asr-001482
02:13:57.100 --> 02:14:02.380
Rep. Brian Poe: So that probably explains why until now the release has not yet been approved.

asr-001483
02:14:02.980 --> 02:14:05.560
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So that's what I do not understand.

asr-001484
02:14:06.080 --> 02:14:15.120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Bakit po inabot tayo ng third quarter of this year to complete the requirements for something that is due and demandable since 2024?

asr-001485
02:14:15.120 --> 02:14:18.180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Can you make me understand?

asr-001489
02:14:34.620 --> 02:14:40.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Why? Why wasn't it submitted? We already knew that this was going to be a project.

asr-001492
02:14:45.620 --> 02:14:47.620
Rep. Brian Poe: So it turns out that

asr-001494
02:14:48.620 --> 02:14:56.880
Rep. Brian Poe: The reason why there was a delay in the submission of the necessary documents was they needed to compile the requirements from the suppliers, etc.

asr-001495
02:14:57.060 --> 02:14:59.980
Rep. Brian Poe: And they were only able to do so later this year.

asr-001496
02:15:00.000 --> 02:15:05.720
Rep. Brian Poe: So, the delay is a mix of agency as well as suppliers.

asr-001497
02:15:11.340 --> 02:15:21.000
Rep. Roberto Nazal: What I cannot understand is that the DICT should be the number one digital agency in our country.

asr-001498
02:15:21.620 --> 02:15:24.100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kayo po ang lead sa lahat.

asr-001499
02:15:24.540 --> 02:15:28.820
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, dapat po, kung meron man madi-delay, hindi po dapat kayo.

asr-001500
02:15:28.820 --> 02:15:32.060
Rep. Brian Poe: Dear colleague, I completely understand where you're coming from.

asr-001501
02:15:32.840 --> 02:15:39.820
Rep. Brian Poe: If there's any agency that should move quickly on a digitalized procurement and documentation process, it should be the DICT.

asr-001502
02:15:41.200 --> 02:15:46.820
Rep. Brian Poe: So, I believe I can get a commitment from the agency that they will improve their procurement processes.

asr-001503
02:15:48.220 --> 02:15:55.580
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Saka po, you know, distinguished sponsor, you know how easy it is now to review everything. We have AI.

asr-001504
02:15:57.200 --> 02:15:58.580
Rep. Brian Poe: But I hope...

asr-001505
02:15:58.820 --> 02:16:05.020
Rep. Brian Poe: I know that the DICT is going to work towards better digitalization in terms of its bureaucracy.

asr-001506
02:16:05.540 --> 02:16:13.200
Rep. Brian Poe: Pero sana din pati yung suppliers ng DICT, dito tayo abot sa compatibility ng data.

asr-001507
02:16:13.740 --> 02:16:20.480
Rep. Brian Poe: So, sana yung mga suppliers din ng DICT are up to standard in terms of their digitization para wala ng bottleneck.

asr-001508
02:16:20.980 --> 02:16:21.940
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Yes, I agree.

asr-001509
02:16:21.940 --> 02:16:28.760
Rep. Roberto Nazal: But of course, my understanding is that if you look at the way the DICT is paying,

asr-001510
02:16:28.820 --> 02:16:33.800
Rep. Roberto Nazal: walang supplier na magsusurvive sa ganitong sitwasyon.

asr-001511
02:16:34.640 --> 02:16:39.660
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, the suppliers are effectively front-loading everything.

asr-001512
02:16:41.080 --> 02:16:50.320
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, I understand that this disincentivizes some of our suppliers and potential investors

asr-001513
02:16:50.320 --> 02:16:56.640
Rep. Brian Poe: if this is how our lead digital agency deals with its documentation and disbursement processes.

asr-001514
02:16:56.640 --> 02:16:58.120
Rep. Brian Poe: But rest assured,

asr-001515
02:16:58.820 --> 02:17:04.840
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, within this year, this outstanding balance should be settled by the DICT.

asr-001516
02:17:11.080 --> 02:17:19.520
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, if I may also note that 90% of cash downloaded by the DBM has already been utilized.

asr-001517
02:17:19.520 --> 02:17:23.880
Rep. Brian Poe: So, it's really just a question of whether or not the funding is downloaded.

asr-001518
02:17:24.080 --> 02:17:27.220
Rep. Brian Poe: Once it is, it's immediately utilized by the agency.

asr-001519
02:17:27.340 --> 02:17:28.520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, it's really a factor.

asr-001520
02:17:28.820 --> 02:17:29.360
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, it's really a funding issue.

asr-001521
02:17:31.360 --> 02:17:35.120
Rep. Brian Poe: Yeah, I would say that a big chunk of it would be.

asr-001522
02:17:36.180 --> 02:17:41.220
Rep. Brian Poe: And I hope that this can be streamlined on the agency side.

asr-001523
02:17:41.220 --> 02:17:46.020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, let us now go to earmarked funds.

asr-001524
02:17:47.500 --> 02:17:50.300
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor,

asr-001525
02:17:51.080 --> 02:17:55.320
Rep. Roberto Nazal: separate from the regular budget of DICT,

asr-001526
02:17:56.000 --> 02:17:57.940
Rep. Roberto Nazal: ano naman ang absorptive capacity?

asr-001527
02:17:58.820 --> 02:18:02.100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: ng DICT when it comes to earmarked funds?

asr-001528
02:18:06.660 --> 02:18:11.840
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Lagi kasi namin kayong pinaglalaban because digitalization needs money.

asr-001529
02:18:12.580 --> 02:18:13.360
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And I know that.

asr-001530
02:18:13.360 --> 02:18:20.300
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And if we should be spending on anything, it should be, we should prioritize the digital infrastructure.

asr-001531
02:18:21.080 --> 02:18:28.280
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Pero kung may malaking problema, yung earmarked balance naman at hindi ninyo nagagastos, ano ba ang problema?

asr-001532
02:18:28.820 --> 02:18:37.100
Rep. Brian Poe: In terms of the earmarked funds, Madam Speaker, we're talking about the free Wi-Fi.

asr-001533
02:18:37.100 --> 02:18:42.440
Rep. Brian Poe: And that's at 61% in terms of utilization.

asr-001534
02:18:44.180 --> 02:18:50.320
Rep. Brian Poe: So, that speaks to the absorptive capacity of the agency to be able to utilize the earmarked funds.

asr-001535
02:18:51.200 --> 02:18:52.100
Rep. Brian Poe: But yes, 61%.

asr-001536
02:18:52.740 --> 02:18:58.420
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And that is what I cannot reconcile, Distinguished Sponsor, Madam Speaker.

asr-001537
02:18:58.820 --> 02:19:05.420
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Twelve digital systems hosted on the E-Gov PH were temporarily disabled

asr-001538
02:19:05.420 --> 02:19:09.480
Rep. Roberto Nazal: because DICT could not pay for cloud server space.

asr-001539
02:19:10.480 --> 02:19:12.880
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Twelve government systems went down.

asr-001540
02:19:14.280 --> 02:19:15.340
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, meron kayong pera.

asr-001541
02:19:16.140 --> 02:19:17.060
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Paano po nangyari ito?

asr-001542
02:19:17.980 --> 02:19:19.000
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Ano ba nangyari talaga?

asr-001543
02:19:19.120 --> 02:19:21.080
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Can you explain?

asr-001544
02:19:21.920 --> 02:19:23.280
Rep. Roberto Nazal: How much was unpaid?

asr-001545
02:19:24.100 --> 02:19:24.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: To whom?

asr-001546
02:19:25.140 --> 02:19:26.720
Rep. Roberto Nazal: How long were the systems down?

asr-001547
02:19:26.720 --> 02:19:27.140
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Down.

asr-001548
02:19:27.700 --> 02:19:28.720
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And was this all...

asr-001549
02:19:28.820 --> 02:19:29.860
Rep. Roberto Nazal: It's also an NCA problem.

asr-001550
02:19:47.980 --> 02:19:49.360
Rep. Brian Poe: Yung time,

asr-001551
02:19:49.460 --> 02:19:57.180
Rep. Brian Poe: It went down because, Madam Speaker, dear colleague, we had a surge of 700% in terms of its use.

asr-001552
02:19:57.720 --> 02:19:58.800
Rep. Brian Poe: So, the systems weren't...

asr-001553
02:19:58.820 --> 02:20:01.100
Rep. Brian Poe: We weren't able to handle that much.

asr-001554
02:20:02.140 --> 02:20:05.060
Rep. Brian Poe: And therefore, the systems went down for a short period of time.

asr-001555
02:20:10.140 --> 02:20:20.740
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, it was only down for five hours on day one and six hours on day two.

asr-001556
02:20:21.580 --> 02:20:28.060
Rep. Brian Poe: But this is definitely because no one was able to predict a 700% surge in the use.

asr-001557
02:20:29.700 --> 02:20:33.320
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Paano po ba nangyari yung surge?

asr-001558
02:20:33.800 --> 02:20:41.220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: I mean, during that day or the day before that or the month before, ilan na ba yung gumagamit?

asr-001559
02:20:50.860 --> 02:20:54.500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, was it only on that day na talagang nagkaroon ng surge?

asr-001560
02:20:55.080 --> 02:20:56.880
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And the capacity could not absorb it?

asr-001561
02:20:57.340 --> 02:20:58.660
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, it...

asr-001562
02:20:58.660 --> 02:20:59.260
Rep. Brian Poe: It turns...

asr-001563
02:20:59.260 --> 02:21:10.440
Rep. Brian Poe: Mr. Speaker, it turns out that the cloud services ended up running out of credits because of the overuse.

asr-001564
02:21:10.440 --> 02:21:13.140
Rep. Brian Poe: And that's how we ended up with that surge.

asr-001565
02:21:14.620 --> 02:21:15.400
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Running out of credit.

asr-001566
02:21:16.020 --> 02:21:18.340
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, that means, hindi po natin...

asr-001567
02:21:18.340 --> 02:21:25.300
Rep. Roberto Nazal: We didn't have enough cash or money allotted for the capacity.

asr-001568
02:21:25.700 --> 02:21:27.440
Rep. Brian Poe: We didn't, Madam Speaker...

asr-001569
02:21:28.660 --> 02:21:38.520
Rep. Brian Poe: We didn't have enough budget enough for the surge that basically no one within the agency predicted that there would be a 700% surge in the use.

asr-001570
02:21:38.960 --> 02:21:42.640
Rep. Brian Poe: And therefore, the cloud services that were contracted weren't enough.

asr-001571
02:21:42.800 --> 02:21:48.340
Rep. Brian Poe: And therefore, we needed to procure more in order to adapt to the capacity required.

asr-001572
02:21:49.740 --> 02:21:55.420
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, that's where I'm puzzled, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-001575
02:21:56.800 --> 02:22:02.700
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Nag-down ang 12 government systems dahil kulang tayo sa pambayad sa cloud.

asr-001576
02:22:04.040 --> 02:22:06.880
Rep. Roberto Nazal: But you have earmarked revenues.

asr-001577
02:22:08.260 --> 02:22:15.180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Meron po kayong pera na dapat kayo mismo ay may access doon at madali niyong magamit.

asr-001578
02:22:15.560 --> 02:22:19.020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And this is for free Wi-Fi and for our cloud services.

asr-001579
02:22:19.880 --> 02:22:20.120
Rep. Brian Poe: Yes.

asr-001580
02:22:20.600 --> 02:22:25.920
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, regarding that concern, that's correct that there are earmarked funds.

asr-001581
02:22:25.920 --> 02:22:27.840
Rep. Brian Poe: I don't...

asr-001582
02:22:27.840 --> 02:22:31.290
Rep. Roberto Nazal: All of it?

asr-001582-split-2
02:22:31.290 --> 02:22:34.040
Rep. Brian Poe: Right.

asr-001583
02:22:34.040 --> 02:22:40.560
Rep. Brian Poe: So, it's not included in the earmarked funds as part of the automatic use.

asr-001584
02:22:41.180 --> 02:22:47.500
Rep. Brian Poe: So, for data, we're unable to use those earmarked funds in order to fund cloud data.

asr-001585
02:22:48.500 --> 02:22:51.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Are we expecting this to happen again?

asr-001586
02:22:51.040 --> 02:22:57.320
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Or do we have enough funds already and credits, so-called credits, to cover any surge in the future?

asr-001587
02:22:57.880 --> 02:22:58.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And do...

asr-001588
02:22:58.540 --> 02:23:02.580
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Do we have access to the earmarked funds para hindi na ito mangyari ulit?

asr-001589
02:23:02.580 --> 02:23:10.420
Rep. Brian Poe: So based on the eGov law, Madam Speaker, we do have enough funds to maintain.

asr-001590
02:23:11.600 --> 02:23:15.460
Rep. Brian Poe: But that doesn't necessarily mean that we are at optimal.

asr-001591
02:23:15.900 --> 02:23:20.580
Rep. Brian Poe: If I'm not mistaken, the budget that we're being given for these cloud services...

asr-001592
02:23:21.100 --> 02:23:25.300
Rep. Brian Poe: I mean, for our data services is about 949 million.

asr-001593
02:23:26.080 --> 02:23:27.580
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: For the indulgence of...

asr-001595
02:23:27.880 --> 02:23:31.780
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: For the honorable Nazal, if he could kindly wind up.

asr-001596
02:23:32.580 --> 02:23:32.860
Rep. Brian Poe: Right.

asr-001597
02:23:33.040 --> 02:23:35.820
Rep. Brian Poe: So, 949 million for eGov.

asr-001598
02:23:35.960 --> 02:23:40.920
Rep. Brian Poe: But the reality is, we actually need additional funds for redundancies.

asr-001599
02:23:41.160 --> 02:23:47.760
Rep. Brian Poe: We need additional funds for emergency systems, which we don't have currently.

asr-001600
02:23:48.200 --> 02:23:51.060
Rep. Brian Poe: So, if you're wondering why there's a risk of it going down,

asr-001601
02:23:51.360 --> 02:23:54.860
Rep. Brian Poe: it's partly because we're underfunding this specific program.

asr-001602
02:23:54.860 --> 02:23:57.760
Rep. Brian Poe: But the law does provide for the bare minimum required.

asr-001603
02:23:57.880 --> 02:24:00.800
Rep. Brian Poe: to operate and maintain eGov.

asr-001604
02:24:00.800 --> 02:24:05.860
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, what is the funding actually needed for us to be able to support?

asr-001605
02:24:10.740 --> 02:24:14.520
Rep. Brian Poe: The request is 1.8 billion, Madam Speaker.

asr-001606
02:24:15.940 --> 02:24:20.120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, bakit pa po natin kunin ito sa USF?

asr-001607
02:24:20.120 --> 02:24:22.120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Um...

asr-001608
02:24:22.120 --> 02:24:24.120
Rep. Brian Poe: Because...

asr-001609
02:24:24.880 --> 02:24:26.120
Rep. Brian Poe: ...

asr-001610
02:24:27.880 --> 02:24:36.040
Rep. Brian Poe: Well, that's a very valid point that the USF could possibly be used,

asr-001611
02:24:36.100 --> 02:24:39.440
Rep. Brian Poe: or earmarked funds could possibly be used for cloud services.

asr-001612
02:24:39.860 --> 02:24:45.400
Rep. Brian Poe: However, unfortunately, that is not within the purview of the agency to decide that.

asr-001613
02:24:45.820 --> 02:24:50.600
Rep. Brian Poe: I believe that is a call of the DBM, if I'm not mistaken, Madam Speaker.

asr-001614
02:24:50.600 --> 02:24:50.820
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Okay.

asr-001615
02:24:53.520 --> 02:24:57.760
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Maybe due to lack of time, I just have to bring this up.

asr-001616
02:24:58.140 --> 02:25:02.940
Rep. Roberto Nazal: During our previous hearing also, we already discussed that much of the government data is hosted abroad.

asr-001617
02:25:03.400 --> 02:25:07.080
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And that DICT needs local availability zones or data centers.

asr-001618
02:25:08.160 --> 02:25:09.300
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Hindi ko na po ulitin yun.

asr-001619
02:25:09.660 --> 02:25:12.520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Ang follow-up ko lang, kailan matatapos ang migration?

asr-001620
02:25:18.700 --> 02:25:25.080
Rep. Roberto Nazal: What percentage of critical government data and workloads will be locally hosted by end of November 26?

asr-001621
02:25:25.380 --> 02:25:27.440
Rep. Roberto Nazal: By end of November 2027?

asr-001622
02:25:27.880 --> 02:25:30.260
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And when will migration be substantially completed?

asr-001623
02:25:34.000 --> 02:25:39.360
Rep. Brian Poe: By the end of this year, we're looking at 20% of critical government data would be localized.

asr-001624
02:25:40.060 --> 02:25:45.320
Rep. Brian Poe: We currently have one server that is up in Subic.

asr-001625
02:25:46.180 --> 02:25:48.320
Rep. Brian Poe: One data center that's up in Subic.

asr-001626
02:25:48.320 --> 02:25:55.340
Rep. Brian Poe: And we're hoping that we'll be able to localize our government data all by 2028.

asr-001627
02:25:55.980 --> 02:25:57.860
Rep. Brian Poe: That's the goal, Madam Speaker.

asr-001628
02:25:57.880 --> 02:26:01.900
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And how much is needed to localize everything by 2028?

asr-001629
02:26:05.340 --> 02:26:12.200
Rep. Brian Poe: Based on the feasibility studies, DICT is projecting 8 billion in costs, Madam Speaker.

asr-001630
02:26:19.820 --> 02:26:23.880
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Chair, Distinguished Sponsor, I go back to where I started.

asr-001631
02:26:25.460 --> 02:26:27.720
Rep. Roberto Nazal: DICT's mandate is much bigger than Wi-Fi.

asr-001636
02:26:27.800 --> 02:26:30.200
Rep. Roberto Nazal: connectivity, computers and subscriptions.

asr-001637
02:26:31.100 --> 02:26:35.700
Rep. Roberto Nazal: DICT is supposed to lead the digital transformation of government.

asr-001638
02:26:36.580 --> 02:26:42.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: That means efficient ICT spending, reliable e-gov systems, interoperable databases,

asr-001639
02:26:42.880 --> 02:26:46.520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: trusted digital identity, transparent government processes,

asr-001640
02:26:47.380 --> 02:26:52.300
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and public spending that citizens can digitally trace.

asr-001641
02:26:52.860 --> 02:26:57.640
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Lagi naman natin pinaglalaban na mabigyan kayo ng sapat na resources ang DICT,

asr-001642
02:26:57.880 --> 02:27:19.840
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Because digitalization is essential. But if you need more money, tell Congress exactly what you need and what it will deliver. And if the money is already available, particularly from earmarked resources, then we need to understand why it is not being converted into reliable government services. Thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-001643
02:27:19.840 --> 02:27:31.000
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, I want to thank our colleague for his constructive questions. They're very valid and they really point to the needs of the agency.

asr-001644
02:27:35.000 --> 02:27:36.140
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

asr-001645
02:27:37.280 --> 02:27:49.780
Rep. Jonathan Keith T. Flores: To further interpellate on the proposed budget, Madam Speaker, I move that we recognize the representative of Kabataan Party-list,

asr-001646
02:27:49.840 --> 02:27:53.300
Rep. Jonathan Keith T. Flores: Representative Renee Louise Co.

asr-001647
02:27:54.160 --> 02:27:59.280
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Honorable Renee Louise Co of Kabataan Party-list is hereby recognized for her interpellation.

asr-001648
02:28:00.080 --> 02:28:07.180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Madam Chair. And good evening to our distinguished sponsor and to DICT.

asr-001649
02:28:07.980 --> 02:28:17.640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So may this distinguished sponsor yield to a couple of questions regarding the budget of DICT?

asr-001650
02:28:18.040 --> 02:28:19.640
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, it would be my privilege.

asr-001651
02:28:19.840 --> 02:28:23.020
Rep. Brian Poe: It would be my privilege to answer the questions of my dear colleague.

asr-001652
02:28:23.560 --> 02:28:25.220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001653
02:28:25.820 --> 02:28:34.040
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor, my first line of questioning would be in relation to the free public internet access program,

asr-001654
02:28:34.280 --> 02:28:40.580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: which this representation thanks the DICT for the report that it has provided,

asr-001655
02:28:40.580 --> 02:28:49.220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: giving more detail as to which locations, which schools, which SUCs have already,

asr-001656
02:28:49.840 --> 02:28:58.020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: established connections for free public internet access, and which ones are yet to be established.

asr-001657
02:28:58.440 --> 02:29:08.080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So we've noted that for basic and secondary public educational institutions,

asr-001658
02:29:08.780 --> 02:29:16.980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: there are more unconnected public schools in Region 5, more than in other regions.

asr-001659
02:29:16.980 --> 02:29:19.820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May we ask, perhaps, why this is so?

asr-001660
02:29:19.840 --> 02:29:28.900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Is there a greater difficulty in accessing regions or locations in Region 5, for example?

asr-001661
02:29:34.440 --> 02:29:39.300
Rep. Brian Poe: So it's actually not necessarily a technical difficulty.

asr-001662
02:29:39.560 --> 02:29:48.320
Rep. Brian Poe: It's more of a prioritization from DepEd on which areas would receive, I guess, the services first and get connected.

asr-001663
02:29:49.840 --> 02:29:59.760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So is it to say that there's no one explanation as to why there's this number of unconnected public schools?

asr-001665
02:30:00.000 --> 02:30:16.180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, we just noted that in Region 5, there's 70 locations that are being targeted to put up an internet connection or a free internet connection for, which is more than the other regions.

asr-001666
02:30:16.180 --> 02:30:28.480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: For example, the next region which has more number of locations na kailangan ng connection would be already NIR at 38.

asr-001667
02:30:28.480 --> 02:30:36.980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, yung 70 ng Region 5, it just stands out. So, meron po bang particular reason? If any, Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001668
02:30:46.080 --> 02:30:54.460
Rep. Brian Poe: Okay. So, out of the 45,000 target schools of DepEd, 11,000 were connected by DICT.

asr-001669
02:30:54.460 --> 02:30:58.460
Rep. Brian Poe: However, the remaining were supposedly already connected by...

asr-001670
02:30:58.480 --> 02:31:03.860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, parang may connection na po. Ganon. So, hindi priority.

asr-001671
02:31:03.860 --> 02:31:13.100
Rep. Brian Poe: There should be a connection. Although, what I know, dear colleague, is that there are some areas wherein they were connected and now there are problems with connection.

asr-001672
02:31:13.660 --> 02:31:21.380
Rep. Brian Poe: And there are other areas from based on testimonies I've heard in which they don't have connection or are requesting for connection still.

asr-001673
02:31:21.380 --> 02:31:27.840
Rep. Brian Poe: So, while the numbers reported to us is that on paper, we know that we have high connectivity.

asr-001674
02:31:28.480 --> 02:31:31.240
Rep. Brian Poe: And that there are several areas that have been connected and we're...

asr-001675
02:31:31.240 --> 02:31:33.340
Rep. Brian Poe: What's the DepEd number? We're at 90%?

asr-001676
02:31:36.160 --> 02:31:40.160
Rep. Brian Poe: We're at 99.39% in terms of connectivity.

asr-001677
02:31:41.340 --> 02:31:48.120
Rep. Brian Poe: However, and this is where I need the help of my colleagues as well as the other members who are present.

asr-001678
02:31:48.940 --> 02:31:57.560
Rep. Brian Poe: If you could give me a list of all the schools that don't have access, aren't connected, or were connected and lost their connection,

asr-001690
02:31:57.800 --> 02:32:07.760
Rep. Brian Poe: And I would gladly work with my colleague to call the attention of DICT to make sure that these areas are reconnected or are connected as per the mandate of DICT.

asr-001691
02:32:08.340 --> 02:32:10.960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you for that opening, Madam Speaker.

asr-001692
02:32:11.100 --> 02:32:11.600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Good sponsor.

asr-001693
02:32:12.240 --> 02:32:22.600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At the proper time, this representation would also like to submit any of the information and requests that it has gathered regarding that.

asr-001694
02:32:22.600 --> 02:32:28.120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But in relation to that point, at ito rin po yung nakalagay sa report na,

asr-001695
02:32:28.480 --> 02:32:41.660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na ilahad ng DICT that the NEP for fiscal year 2027 provides for the maintenance and operation of more than 16,000 free Wi-Fi locations established in 2026.

asr-001696
02:32:41.660 --> 02:32:51.660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But to ensure the continued availability of free Wi-Fi in public schools, an additional 3 billion is necessary for the maintenance and operation of existing school sites.

asr-001697
02:32:52.020 --> 02:32:58.460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At iba pa yung tier 2 budget request na 10 billion plus for the expansion of free Wi-Fi to other priorities.

asr-001698
02:32:58.480 --> 02:33:00.720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: public service locations. So to clarify

asr-001699
02:33:00.720 --> 02:33:02.720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, Good Sponsor, itong

asr-001700
02:33:02.720 --> 02:33:04.500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: 3 billion, additional 3 billion

asr-001701
02:33:04.500 --> 02:33:06.500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: for the continued

asr-001702
02:33:06.500 --> 02:33:08.620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: availability, hindi pa po ito granted?

asr-001703
02:33:09.660 --> 02:33:10.180
Rep. Brian Poe: Yes.

asr-001704
02:33:10.780 --> 02:33:11.240
Rep. Brian Poe: Hindi pa.

asr-001705
02:33:11.840 --> 02:33:14.840
Rep. Brian Poe: Hindi pa granted because the only thing that I'm sure

asr-001706
02:33:14.840 --> 02:33:16.100
Rep. Brian Poe: will be granted

asr-001707
02:33:16.100 --> 02:33:18.640
Rep. Brian Poe: is the continuing appropriation

asr-001708
02:33:18.640 --> 02:33:20.620
Rep. Brian Poe: from the spectrum user fee, which

asr-001709
02:33:20.620 --> 02:33:22.560
Rep. Brian Poe: is the earmark fund for free WiFi.

asr-001710
02:33:23.080 --> 02:33:24.300
Rep. Brian Poe: But the additional funds,

asr-001711
02:33:24.640 --> 02:33:26.920
