02:44:02.660 --> 02:44:10.440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pero at least sa DICT, gusto po natin makita yung mga detalye ng paano po niroroll out niya yung mga kurso na ito.

asr-001901
02:44:10.700 --> 02:44:12.300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Would that be...

asr-001902
02:44:12.300 --> 02:44:13.980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Can that happen, Madam Speaker?

asr-001903
02:44:13.980 --> 02:44:14.460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Good sponsor.

asr-001904
02:44:15.300 --> 02:44:20.580
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, to be fair, the mandate of DICT would be on the capacity building side,

asr-001905
02:44:20.580 --> 02:44:22.940
Rep. Brian Poe: but not necessarily the immediate employment.

asr-001906
02:44:23.120 --> 02:44:30.060
Rep. Brian Poe: However, that doesn't mean that it shouldn't be a priority for DICT to make sure that they're highly employable after their programs.

asr-001907
02:44:30.400 --> 02:44:35.300
Rep. Brian Poe: With that being said, I have the commitment of the Secretary that we can provide to you, to this representation,

asr-001908
02:44:35.980 --> 02:44:45.060
Rep. Brian Poe: the framework that was used to create this program, and also, if my colleague has any constituents,

asr-001909
02:44:45.060 --> 02:44:49.580
Rep. Brian Poe: that would like to participate in any of the capacity building activities,

asr-001910
02:44:50.780 --> 02:44:56.760
Rep. Brian Poe: the DICT has given their commitment to immediately enroll and add them into the program

asr-001911
02:44:56.760 --> 02:44:59.980
Rep. Brian Poe: so that you can get first-hand experience on these programs.

asr-001912
02:45:00.000 --> 02:45:07.420
Rep. Brian Poe: and also give your critique on whether or not this is really effective in providing ang mga kabataan natin ng mas maraming oportunidad.

asr-001913
02:45:08.420 --> 02:45:09.900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Madam Speaker, Good Sponsor.

asr-001914
02:45:10.300 --> 02:45:16.800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I am of the understanding that there are slots that are allotted to various enterprises.

asr-001915
02:45:17.700 --> 02:45:23.340
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, we might have to consult also with these regions, etc.

asr-001916
02:45:23.340 --> 02:45:30.560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But nonetheless, we appreciate the details of the qualitative framework by which this upskilling happens.

asr-001917
02:45:31.100 --> 02:45:41.560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Lalo na po yung pangamba ng karamihan ng ating mga employees in different sectors, lalo na sa BPO, kung saan mas inaasahan yung upskilling na itong mangyari,

asr-001918
02:45:41.560 --> 02:45:50.260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: rather than AI integration helping these employees to further their careers,

asr-001919
02:45:50.400 --> 02:45:53.320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ay nagiging rason pa nga po na sila ay maaari.

asr-001920
02:45:53.340 --> 02:45:55.740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ma-retrench, ma-let go.

asr-001921
02:45:56.140 --> 02:46:04.600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Sila po ay nawawalan ng trabaho because of the further integration of AI in these companies' workflows.

asr-001922
02:46:05.060 --> 02:46:09.800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But nonetheless, Madam Speaker, Good Sponsor, we will be waiting for the submission of the Good Department.

asr-001923
02:46:10.280 --> 02:46:15.160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: My last question would be in relation to the EGOV PH app.

asr-001924
02:46:15.160 --> 02:46:23.000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I remember in the presentation of the DICT that there are 54 million users registered as of date.

asr-001925
02:46:23.340 --> 02:46:32.540
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: During the presentation, may we ask, yung breakdown nito, ilan po ba dito sa 54 million users ang unique Filipino users?

asr-001926
02:46:33.260 --> 02:46:35.940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I assume dahil po may ilan po dito.

asr-001927
02:46:35.940 --> 02:46:40.940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mga foreigners, nirequire na i-download yung EGOV app para po sa kanilang mga travel details.

asr-001928
02:46:42.860 --> 02:46:47.320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May ilan dito foreigners? So ilan po sa 54 million users nito ang Pilipino?

asr-001929
02:46:53.340 --> 02:47:02.900
Rep. Brian Poe: So from the DICT is claiming that only 3 to 4 percent of these active users are foreigners.

asr-001930
02:47:03.680 --> 02:47:06.680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Okay. So most of them are Filipino users po?

asr-001931
02:47:07.080 --> 02:47:10.920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Okay. And we are sure naman po na unique users sila.

asr-001932
02:47:10.920 --> 02:47:16.400
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I assume dahil may IDs din pong pinapasubmit para magka-EGOV account.

asr-001933
02:47:16.940 --> 02:47:20.760
Rep. Brian Poe: Yes, Madam Speaker, we can guarantee that these are unique accounts.

asr-001934
02:47:21.260 --> 02:47:21.400
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Okay.

asr-001935
02:47:22.300 --> 02:47:23.260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker...

asr-001936
02:47:23.340 --> 02:47:31.500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor, may data ba kung anong mga services yung mga ginagamit ng mga Filipino users natin?

asr-001937
02:47:31.920 --> 02:47:36.280
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Alin po yung mas frequently ginagamit versus sa hindi pa nagagamit?

asr-001938
02:47:44.720 --> 02:47:50.260
Rep. Brian Poe: If we could just have a quick second to confer kung ano yung mga top services na ginagamit.

asr-001939
02:47:50.720 --> 02:47:53.000
Rep. Brian Poe: But one thing I want to point out is unlike...

asr-001940
02:47:53.340 --> 02:47:55.700
Rep. Brian Poe: Social media, these are unique accounts.

asr-001941
02:47:56.480 --> 02:47:56.920
Rep. Brian Poe: Yes.

asr-001942
02:47:56.920 --> 02:47:59.880
Rep. Brian Poe: So that we can verify due to their government IDs.

asr-001943
02:48:01.640 --> 02:48:04.160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I ask these questions, Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001944
02:48:04.600 --> 02:48:09.180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And I will allow the distinguished sponsor the few moments to confer with DICT.

asr-001945
02:48:09.180 --> 02:48:21.920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Para po maitimbang din natin yung dami ng pera na binibigay natin sa EGOV app development and maintenance.

asr-001946
02:48:22.260 --> 02:48:23.180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Sa paano ba...

asr-001947
02:48:23.340 --> 02:48:27.680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pag ginagamit, gaano ba kadalas na nagagamit ng mga mamamayan natin yung app?

asr-001948
02:48:28.380 --> 02:48:30.880
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Paano ba siya na ma-maximize, if any, or hindi?

asr-001949
02:48:31.820 --> 02:48:35.920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Yun po yung gusto nating ma-test with this data point, perhaps.

asr-001950
02:48:35.920 --> 02:48:41.360
Rep. Brian Poe: So I have the breakdown, Madam Speaker.

asr-001951
02:48:42.080 --> 02:48:50.800
Rep. Brian Poe: First is national ID, followed by PhilHealth, followed by Pag-ibig, followed by e-travel,

asr-001952
02:48:51.540 --> 02:48:53.300
Rep. Brian Poe: which is then followed by clearance.

asr-001953
02:48:53.340 --> 02:48:58.420
Rep. Brian Poe: Permits, social services, and last would be the health desk.

asr-001954
02:48:59.420 --> 02:49:05.840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor, may this representation receive a report on the breakdown of services use?

asr-001955
02:49:06.480 --> 02:49:14.620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And maybe kung this data is available, how much of the percentage of Filipino users that are registered,

asr-001956
02:49:15.100 --> 02:49:16.980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ang gumagamit ng mga servisyong ito?

asr-001957
02:49:17.420 --> 02:49:19.320
Rep. Brian Poe: We will request for that.

asr-001958
02:49:19.760 --> 02:49:23.180
Rep. Brian Poe: The agency is committing that they will submit the percentages.

asr-001959
02:49:23.340 --> 02:49:26.600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And last question, Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001960
02:49:28.140 --> 02:49:34.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Saan po nakastore ang data na kinakalap ng e-gov app?

asr-001961
02:49:36.860 --> 02:49:39.000
Rep. Brian Poe: Singapore and the United States.

asr-001962
02:49:39.600 --> 02:49:43.740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So it's at data centers of Singapore and United States.

asr-001963
02:49:44.100 --> 02:49:48.680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So we're availing of cloud services para po makuha sila?

asr-001964
02:49:49.460 --> 02:49:53.320
Rep. Brian Poe: Yes, Madam Speaker, I can confirm that we are using cloud services.

asr-001965
02:49:53.340 --> 02:49:54.720
Rep. Brian Poe: In order to host this data.

asr-001966
02:49:55.580 --> 02:50:01.000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: How much data po ang nakalap na para po sa e-gov PH?

asr-001967
02:50:01.140 --> 02:50:03.320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Like terabytes na po ba ito, Madam Speaker, good sponsor?

asr-001968
02:50:12.540 --> 02:50:15.980
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Speaker, six terabytes of data.

asr-001969
02:50:17.800 --> 02:50:22.480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor, we're initially concerned that that's a lot of data.

asr-001970
02:50:22.480 --> 02:50:22.680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Okay.

asr-001971
02:50:23.340 --> 02:50:28.960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: That's all personal data of Filipinos that's not hosted in the Philippines.

asr-001972
02:50:29.540 --> 02:50:39.140
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So mayhaps the department may consider some way to locally host this data.

asr-001973
02:50:39.720 --> 02:50:43.220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Lalo na maaari kung magkaroon ng data breach.

asr-001974
02:50:43.920 --> 02:50:46.460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May mga assurances na binigay ang DICT publicly.

asr-001975
02:50:47.040 --> 02:50:50.980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But nonetheless, hindi siya foolproof guarantee that it won't happen.

asr-001976
02:50:50.980 --> 02:50:52.020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Lalo na po.

asr-001977
02:50:53.340 --> 02:50:56.360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At hindi po siya stored locally.

asr-001978
02:50:57.000 --> 02:50:58.880
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So siguro na lang po.

asr-001979
02:50:59.220 --> 02:51:01.600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: A final response on that point, Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-001980
02:51:01.720 --> 02:51:02.680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And I have no further questions.

asr-001981
02:51:09.720 --> 02:51:11.240
Rep. Brian Poe: So I stand corrected.

asr-001982
02:51:11.420 --> 02:51:14.520
Rep. Brian Poe: It's 60 terabytes, not just 6 terabytes, Madam Speaker.

asr-001983
02:51:14.740 --> 02:51:16.440
Rep. Brian Poe: And my colleague is correct.

asr-001984
02:51:16.780 --> 02:51:22.300
Rep. Brian Poe: We actually, based on the eGov law, are supposed to move towards localization of data

asr-001986
02:51:23.320 --> 02:51:25.420
Rep. Brian Poe: By 2028, I believe, is the commitment.

asr-001987
02:51:26.080 --> 02:51:30.340
Rep. Brian Poe: And we need another 8 billion pesos to be able to get there.

asr-001988
02:51:30.820 --> 02:51:33.640
Rep. Brian Poe: And that's the conservative estimate from the DICT.

asr-001989
02:51:34.480 --> 02:51:38.840
Rep. Brian Poe: We've already allocated it, if I'm not mistaken, 9 billion so far.

asr-001990
02:51:39.240 --> 02:51:46.580
Rep. Brian Poe: We've allocated 9 billion over the course of 8 years

asr-001991
02:51:46.580 --> 02:51:51.580
Rep. Brian Poe: in order to address the data storage issue.

asr-001992
02:51:51.580 --> 02:51:52.720
Rep. Brian Poe: But again,

asr-001993
02:51:53.320 --> 02:51:58.680
Rep. Brian Poe: moving towards 2028, we need another 8 billion to reach our target.

asr-001994
02:51:59.140 --> 02:52:04.860
Rep. Brian Poe: So I actually have the breakdown of the appropriation for data center

asr-001995
02:52:04.860 --> 02:52:09.120
Rep. Brian Poe: from 2016 until our 2027 NEP.

asr-001996
02:52:09.600 --> 02:52:19.680
Rep. Brian Poe: The total amount between MOE and capital outlay is 9,572,567 pesos.

asr-001997
02:52:20.460 --> 02:52:23.120
Rep. Brian Poe: And then, of course, we need another 8 billion to reach our target.

asr-002000
