Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: na depende kung nasan ka,

asr-004738
05:05:24.700 --> 05:05:28.740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ay mas pababa ang sweldo kahit pareho naman.

asr-004739
05:05:29.360 --> 05:05:36.160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Walang measurable and objective na kaibahan sa cost of living.

asr-004740
05:05:36.860 --> 05:05:38.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yan po ang problema.

asr-004741
05:05:39.100 --> 05:05:39.780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi po ba ganun?

asr-004742
05:05:40.520 --> 05:05:48.120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At hindi ba panahon na para ma-abolish ang sistema nito ng regional wage setting?

asr-004743
05:05:50.840 --> 05:05:54.020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, I get your point.

asr-004744
05:05:54.700 --> 05:06:01.240
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Distinguished colleague, na pag talon mo sa isang lugar na isang bayan ay iba na yung rate.

asr-004745
05:06:02.300 --> 05:06:04.680
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And you gave perfect examples of those in which.

asr-004746
05:06:06.480 --> 05:06:12.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: But the thing is, the mandate which was given by Congress sa Department of Labor and Employment,

asr-004747
05:06:13.300 --> 05:06:17.460
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ay kami naman po ay sumusunod sa alituntunin sa pag-set ng minimum wage.

asr-004748
05:06:17.900 --> 05:06:22.940
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: One, yung binigit niyo po kanina ay patungo dun sa we have to also take in consideration

asr-004749
05:06:22.940 --> 05:06:24.480
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: sa dun sa ating income classes.

asr-004750
05:06:24.700 --> 05:06:26.340
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ng Department of Finance.

asr-004751
05:06:26.740 --> 05:06:29.220
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And the most important one is yung productivity.

asr-004752
05:06:30.240 --> 05:06:34.640
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Iba-iba po kasi yung kada bayan, kada reyon, kada probinsya.

asr-004753
05:06:35.600 --> 05:06:39.620
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And patukol naman po dun sa huling statement po ninyo,

asr-004754
05:06:40.260 --> 05:06:44.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na kung napapanahon na po ba pag-abolish dun sa mga different rates.

asr-004755
05:06:45.400 --> 05:06:51.940
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Again, the official stand of Department of Labor and Employment patungo dun sa ating minimum wage setting

asr-004756
05:06:51.940 --> 05:06:53.440
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: or the reach.

asr-004757
05:06:54.700 --> 05:07:05.440
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: RA 6727 or Wage Rationalization Act ay we submit to the wisdom ng ating Kongreso at Senado.

asr-004758
05:07:05.860 --> 05:07:11.120
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Once halimbawang nakapagpasa po ng isang bill or maging ganap na isang batas,

asr-004759
05:07:11.980 --> 05:07:16.920
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: the Department will fully implement kung sakasakaling ito ay maging isang ganap na batas,

asr-004760
05:07:17.180 --> 05:07:18.480
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague.

asr-004761
05:07:19.180 --> 05:07:20.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Well, thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-004762
05:07:20.600 --> 05:07:24.620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang dinidiin po natin talaga, yung patakalan na mismo,

asr-004763
05:07:24.700 --> 05:07:30.960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang pinapakita natin dito na yung pinapatupad na patakalan ng DOLE ng kanilang mga regional wage board

asr-004764
05:07:30.960 --> 05:07:42.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ay, siyempre, alinsunod sa batas, pero pinapakita dito na yung batas ay hindi na naglilingkod sa interes ng mga manggagawang Pilipino.

asr-004765
05:07:43.520 --> 05:07:47.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Maaring pabor sa mga kapitalista. Of course, matutuwa sila.

asr-004766
05:07:48.160 --> 05:07:52.440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Lumipad lang sila ng bayan. Mas mababa na ang kanilang pasweldo.

asr-004767
05:07:52.440 --> 05:07:54.660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero para sa mga mamayang nandun,

asr-004768
05:07:54.700 --> 05:08:00.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: wala namang pinag-iba ang presyo ng bigas ng pagkain sa kabilang bayan.

asr-004769
05:08:00.700 --> 05:08:08.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, again, dinidiin natin panahon na para i-abolish ito at ibalik yung national minimum wage.

asr-004770
05:08:08.700 --> 05:08:15.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Marami pa sana akong datos dyan, kaya lang, pinitingnan ko ang oras, pupunta na ako sa susunod na topic natin.

asr-004771
05:08:15.700 --> 05:08:22.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ang punto natin dito, kapos na kapos na po, at hindi na naglilingkod sa interes at kapakanan ng manggagawa,

asr-004772
05:08:22.700 --> 05:08:23.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang patakarang pinatutupad na ito.

asr-004773
05:08:24.700 --> 05:08:29.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At ang dole, kaugnay sa regionalized, at hindi nga lang regionalized, no,

asr-004774
05:08:29.700 --> 05:08:36.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: municipalized, localized wage setting. Extreme case being Calabarzon.

asr-004775
05:08:36.700 --> 05:08:42.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. So, kailangang ibalik ang national minimum wage.

asr-004776
05:08:42.700 --> 05:08:47.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Ngayon, punta tayo sa usapin ng tupad.

asr-004777
05:08:47.700 --> 05:08:53.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ayan, nabuksan ni, ng naunang interpellator natin, si Representative Eli San Fernando.

asr-004778
05:08:54.700 --> 05:09:04.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At hindi katakataka, dahil nga, kung titignan mo ang budget ng dole, ang pinakamalaking component talaga nito ay tupad.

asr-004779
05:09:04.700 --> 05:09:15.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, pinring up ko na po ito nung budget briefing, but let me revisit the data in plenary.

asr-004780
05:09:15.700 --> 05:09:20.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, kung pwede po, maipakita yung ating presentation.

asr-004781
05:09:20.700 --> 05:09:22.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ayan nga, tinrack nga natin.

asr-004782
05:09:22.700 --> 05:09:27.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung 10 years ng tupad, no, at 2016 yan.

asr-004783
05:09:27.700 --> 05:09:39.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nung 2016, ang level po ng tupad ay nasa, nasa, tupad.

asr-004784
05:09:39.700 --> 05:09:44.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Three, hindi makita.

asr-004785
05:09:44.700 --> 05:09:50.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Is that three?

asr-004786
05:09:50.700 --> 05:09:54.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Is that three?

asr-004787
05:09:54.700 --> 05:09:56.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 3.2 billion.

asr-004788
05:09:56.700 --> 05:09:58.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 3.2 billion pesos po.

asr-004789
05:09:58.700 --> 05:10:00.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: That was 2016.

asr-004790
05:10:00.700 --> 05:10:11.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And then, 2024, 3.2 billion naging 29.5 billion.

asr-004791
05:10:11.700 --> 05:10:16.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No? So, ilang beses na lumaki ito.

asr-004792
05:10:16.700 --> 05:10:18.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Uhm.

asr-004793
05:10:18.700 --> 05:10:25.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: More than, almost 10 times, no, ang paglaki.

asr-004794
05:10:25.700 --> 05:10:29.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yan yung pinakamalaking allocation ng tupad.

asr-004795
05:10:29.700 --> 05:10:36.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: It consists, at that time, it consisted of almost 82% of the total dole budget.

asr-004796
05:10:36.700 --> 05:10:47.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: For 2026, sa kasalukuyang taon, 75% ng budget ng dole, 22 billion pesos ay nasa tupad.

asr-004797
05:10:47.700 --> 05:11:01.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa proposed budget nyo, proposed budget nyo 2027, ayan po, 2027 ay, ah, magkano ang hinihingi?

asr-004798
05:11:01.700 --> 05:11:06.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 14.2 billion o 68% of total.

asr-004799
05:11:06.700 --> 05:11:08.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ayan po ang nasa NEP.

asr-004800
05:11:08.700 --> 05:11:14.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero natatandaan ko rin po sa budget briefing, and maybe it can be stated here on the record,

asr-004801
05:11:14.700 --> 05:11:16.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: humihingi pa po ng dagdad na tupad.

asr-004802
05:11:16.700 --> 05:11:18.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang dole.

asr-004803
05:11:18.700 --> 05:11:28.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pwede po bang ma, ah, banggit for the record kung magkano yung hinihingi ng dole na dagdag sa tupad?

asr-004804
05:11:28.700 --> 05:11:36.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Ah, on record, ah, Madam Speaker Distinguished Colleague, tama po yung sinabi nyo doon sa record na 14.1 billion.

asr-004805
05:11:36.700 --> 05:11:43.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: But for clarity, yung out of that is 3 billion is, ah, GIP, which is the Government Internship Program.

asr-004806
05:11:43.700 --> 05:11:44.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Okay.

asr-004807
05:11:44.700 --> 05:11:51.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: So kung sa inyong tinatanong na kung magkano yung, ah, hinihingi, I mentioned that earlier doon sa ating opening statement,

asr-004808
05:11:51.700 --> 05:11:57.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na kung saan doon sa nakaraang ah, budget ah, hearing sa committee level, I, I think it was 10.1 billion.

asr-004809
05:11:59.700 --> 05:12:00.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: 10.

asr-004810
05:12:01.700 --> 05:12:02.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: 10.25 billion.

asr-004811
05:12:02.700 --> 05:12:03.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 10.4.

asr-004812
05:12:04.700 --> 05:12:05.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 10.25.

asr-004813
05:12:05.700 --> 05:12:06.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Okay, so.

asr-004814
05:12:06.700 --> 05:12:07.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 10.25.

asr-004815
05:12:07.700 --> 05:12:13.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, 14 billion ang nasa NEP, pero gusto niyo po po dagdaga ng mahigit 10 billion.

asr-004816
05:12:13.700 --> 05:12:18.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, gusto niyong gawing 24.8 billion, no?

asr-004817
05:12:18.700 --> 05:12:23.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In other words, halos doblehin yung kasulukuyang hinihingi ng pondo.

asr-004818
05:12:23.700 --> 05:12:26.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ah, yun na nga.

asr-004819
05:12:26.700 --> 05:12:37.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, dinidiinan na natin dito at kinikwestiyon na natin, bakit ang pinakamalaking bahagi ng budget ng dole ay tupad?

asr-004820
05:12:37.700 --> 05:12:38.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

asr-004821
05:12:38.700 --> 05:12:41.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ironically, ah.

asr-004822
05:12:41.700 --> 05:12:45.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, yun nga sabi natin, ano na ba ang dole ngayon?

asr-004823
05:12:46.700 --> 05:12:48.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano ba ang pangunahing mandato ng dole?

asr-004824
05:12:48.700 --> 05:12:51.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, labor and employment?

asr-004825
05:12:52.700 --> 05:12:57.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pagprotekta sa karapatan at kagalingan ng manggagawa?

asr-004826
05:12:57.700 --> 05:13:01.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: O ayuda agency na ba ang dole ngayon?

asr-004827
05:13:01.700 --> 05:13:05.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kasi kung pagbabatayan natin ang budget, ayuda agency na.

asr-004828
05:13:05.700 --> 05:13:06.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

asr-004829
05:13:06.700 --> 05:13:07.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At,

asr-004830
05:13:07.700 --> 05:13:09.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ngayon pa,

asr-004831
05:13:09.700 --> 05:13:10.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: hindi na nagkasya,

asr-004832
05:13:10.700 --> 05:13:18.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: dun sa 14 billion na hinihingi para sa tupad, gusto pang dagdagan ng 10 billion.

asr-004833
05:13:18.700 --> 05:13:19.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

asr-004834
05:13:19.700 --> 05:13:22.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, so,

asr-004835
05:13:22.700 --> 05:13:28.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: paninindigan pa rin ba ng dole ang hinihingi pa nilang dagdag na 10 billion?

asr-004836
05:13:28.700 --> 05:13:29.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Samantala,

asr-004837
05:13:29.700 --> 05:13:33.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: katulad yan ang nasabi, napakaraming mga pangangailangan.

asr-004838
05:13:33.700 --> 05:13:35.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung nabanggit na,

asr-004839
05:13:35.700 --> 05:13:39.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: dagdag na labor inspectors, new plantilla positions,

asr-004840
05:13:39.700 --> 05:13:41.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: for labor inspectors.

asr-004841
05:13:42.700 --> 05:13:43.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bakit hindi?

asr-004842
05:13:43.700 --> 05:13:52.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ilang bagong labor inspectors ang pwedeng madagdagan dun sa 10 billion na hinihingi ninyo?

asr-004843
05:13:52.700 --> 05:13:53.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi po ba?

asr-004844
05:13:53.700 --> 05:14:05.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, paninindigan pa po ba na dagdagan pa sa halip na bawasan ang hinihingi tupad ng dole for 2027?

asr-004845
05:14:06.700 --> 05:14:08.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

asr-004846
05:14:09.700 --> 05:14:11.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: one for the record,

asr-004847
05:14:11.700 --> 05:14:14.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: pagsilabing po po kasing ayuda is dole out.

asr-004848
05:14:14.700 --> 05:14:19.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Ang tupad together with GIP and other the programs of dole.

asr-004849
05:14:19.700 --> 05:14:22.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Yung tupad naman po ay pinagtatrabahuhan.

asr-004850
05:14:22.700 --> 05:14:27.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And if you will allow me, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

asr-004851
05:14:27.700 --> 05:14:32.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: nagkaroon lang kasi because of the pandemic, yung parang stigma doon sa ating tupad.

asr-004852
05:14:32.700 --> 05:14:37.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Pero I'll give you a prime example na isa lamang.

asr-004853
05:14:37.700 --> 05:14:38.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: I'll give you an example.

asr-004854
05:14:39.700 --> 05:14:43.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: In Caloocan, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

asr-004855
05:14:43.700 --> 05:14:50.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: and this is very malapit sa akin to because gustong gusto ko rin gawin ito sa aking distrito.

asr-004856
05:14:50.700 --> 05:14:51.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Bakit?

asr-004857
05:14:51.700 --> 05:14:57.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Yung kanyang under ng tupad, alam naman po natin doon sa reports na na-receive natin sa EDCOM,

asr-004858
05:14:57.700 --> 05:14:59.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na maraming estudyante...

asr-004859
05:15:00.000 --> 05:15:02.560
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: from kinder to grade 10

asr-004860
05:15:02.560 --> 05:15:04.120
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ang medyo nahuhuli

asr-004861
05:15:04.120 --> 05:15:05.920
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: pagdating sa pagbasa

asr-004862
05:15:05.920 --> 05:15:08.040
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: at ang ating resulta

asr-004863
05:15:08.040 --> 05:15:10.120
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ay nahihiyan na po silang pumasok

asr-004864
05:15:10.120 --> 05:15:11.640
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: sa kanilang mga eskwelahan.

asr-004865
05:15:12.640 --> 05:15:13.800
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Ano po ang ginawa ng ating

asr-004866
05:15:13.800 --> 05:15:17.560
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Department of Labor Employment

asr-004867
05:15:17.560 --> 05:15:18.780
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: doon sa Kaloocan?

asr-004868
05:15:19.400 --> 05:15:20.520
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Simpleng-simple lamang.

asr-004869
05:15:21.240 --> 05:15:21.480
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: One,

asr-004870
05:15:22.380 --> 05:15:24.080
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: nag-hire po ang departamento

asr-004871
05:15:24.080 --> 05:15:26.960
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ng mga college graduates

asr-004872
05:15:26.960 --> 05:15:28.840
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: or let passers

asr-004873
05:15:28.840 --> 05:15:29.900
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na hindi pa ganap

asr-004874
05:15:29.900 --> 05:15:31.780
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na hired, na teachers

asr-004875
05:15:31.780 --> 05:15:34.520
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na magtuturo, na magbasa

asr-004876
05:15:34.520 --> 05:15:37.020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: sa ating mga kabataan.

asr-004877
05:15:37.860 --> 05:15:38.740
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: They were employed

asr-004878
05:15:38.740 --> 05:15:40.840
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na ating isandaang

asr-004879
05:15:40.840 --> 05:15:42.540
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: nagtuturo

asr-004880
05:15:42.540 --> 05:15:43.980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: sa ating mga estudyante

asr-004881
05:15:43.980 --> 05:15:46.180
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: sa Kaloocan na kung saan

asr-004882
05:15:46.180 --> 05:15:48.660
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: staggered po 10 days

asr-004883
05:15:48.660 --> 05:15:50.160
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: kasi ang normal

asr-004884
05:15:50.160 --> 05:15:52.020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: and standard na

asr-004885
05:15:52.020 --> 05:15:54.520
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: implementation ng tupad.

asr-004886
05:15:55.020 --> 05:15:56.780
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Doon sa programang ating binabanggit po

asr-004887
05:15:56.780 --> 05:15:58.120
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ito ay ginawang

asr-004888
05:15:58.120 --> 05:15:59.880
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: 30 days na allowable

asr-004889
05:15:59.880 --> 05:16:01.600
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: lamang po sa mga ibang programa.

asr-004890
05:16:01.780 --> 05:16:03.320
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: In short, Madam Speaker,

asr-004891
05:16:04.140 --> 05:16:05.000
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Distinguished Colleague,

asr-004892
05:16:06.120 --> 05:16:08.060
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: yung ginagawa po ng tupad

asr-004893
05:16:08.060 --> 05:16:09.840
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: na stigma noon ay ibang-iba

asr-004894
05:16:09.840 --> 05:16:12.100
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: noon at ngayon.

asr-004895
05:16:12.780 --> 05:16:13.920
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Kasi po, hindi lamang ito

asr-004896
05:16:13.920 --> 05:16:16.060
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: magagamit sa ating mga

asr-004897
05:16:16.060 --> 05:16:17.280
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: streets, but bagkos

asr-004898
05:16:17.280 --> 05:16:20.200
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: ay matuturuan na matuto pa

asr-004899
05:16:20.200 --> 05:16:22.380
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: yung ating mga estudyante

asr-004900
05:16:22.380 --> 05:16:23.760
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: lalong-lalong na

asr-004901
05:16:23.760 --> 05:16:25.280
